    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6447": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Marketing and Communications Specialist",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Marketing and Communications Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Marketing and Communications Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Marketing and Communications Specialist Position Summary The Marketing Communication Specialist contributes to the success of the Marketing and Communications department by contributing to and implementing email campaigns; writing for the university website, blogs and news content; and generally providing writing and support to the Marketing and Communications department. The Marketing Communication Specialist supports a targeted web SEO / GEO strategy and helps produce content accordingly; ensures that email communications and web content are optimized for key conversions and follow rules of grammar, AP Style, visual design and quality assurance. Supervised by Assistant Director of Marketing & Content Development After 180 days of successful employment, this position is potentially a hybrid position (three days/week in office). Schedule established by supervisor. Essential Duties and Responsibilities SEO / GEO Copy Writer Writes and publishes web copy that implements key word optimization for txwes.edu. With supervisor and Director, Digital Media, research potential blog topics that align with the university’s SEO strategy, then writes agreed-upon blog posts for txwes.edu blog. Helps manage the review, editing, and approval of blog posts written by agency partners. With supervisor and Director, Digital Media, maintains and implements both on-page and off-page SEO efforts. Monitors, edits and corrects site content for accuracy, editorial style guidelines (including AP Style) and rules of grammar. Marketing Email Copy Writer Assist the Senior Marketing Manager to write and implement strategic marketing emails in the Slate CRM , ensuring mobile-friendly templates. Ensures that the needed web content is in place to support marketing emails. Understands the admission funnel of each program, including graduate and undergraduate programs, to optimize communication for the target audience. Support Marketing & Communications Projects Support marketing and communications team projects such as: website updates, creative brainstorms, survey creations, copy writing, media communications, etc. Performs other related duties and projects as assigned. Supports creative copy writing efforts of the office of Marketing and Communications including: website content, commercials, email, magazine articles, press releases and digital marketing copy that focus on key conversions and enforces brand identity. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses A Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college with major course work in marketing or a related field. Experience Approximately 1 to 2 years of experience with content management systems ( CMS ) and Customer Relationship Management ( CRM ) systems. Familiarity with the development of effective SEO strategies. Demonstrated understanding of search engine optimization ( SEO ), search engine marketing ( SEM ), and email marketing email best practices. Familiarity with Google Keyword Planner. Experience with copywriting for digital platforms and editing for grammar, spelling and punctuation accuracy, including AP style. Written, verbal, analytical, and organizational skills. Working under tight deadlines and bringing strong attention to detail. Professional copy editing and proofreading. Experience proofreading for website branding standards (fonts, spacing, padding. etc.). Experience in managing a workload including multiple projects and production schedules required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Understanding of SEO fundamentals Digital copywriting ability Ability to write long-form copy for blog posts and website news articles. Understanding of CMS , website technology, and email marketing platforms Knowledge of Associated Press (AP) style guidelines. Understanding of the tools provided by our CMS system and their limitations Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1123P Posting Open Date 07/27/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Portfolio List of Three References Optional Documents 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6339": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Maintenance Mechanic I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Maintenance Mechanic I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Maintenance Mechanic I Position Summary Performs maintenance and repair of building facilities. Must perform tasks that span many trades, including, but not limited to: electrical, mechanical, painting, and plumbing. Must be willing to work overtime as the requirement may rise. Is subject to being recalled to the campus for “after hours” work. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Independently determines the need and performs basic repairs, service and related work on mechanical, plumbing and electrical equipment. 2. Performs scheduled and unscheduled preventive maintenance and adjustments of selected equipment and fixtures as well as operational testing and verification to specific standards. 3. Performs building maintenance tasks, applying an understanding of the University needs as well as the operational and safety limitations of building systems and equipment. 4. Uses various hand and yard tools & equipment to perform assigned tasks. Tests equipment periodically to analyze, evaluate and correct malfunctions with various systems, devices and/or instruments. 5. Completes work orders, equipment logs and other documentation 6. Maintains the work area in a neat, efficient and safe condition by cleaning up after each job and properly storing items and/or test equipment. Exhibits an awareness of safety requirements and practices in everyday tasks. 7. Other duties as assigned. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Must have a valid Texas Drivers license Experience Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Outstanding interpersonal skills with excellent customer service orientation. • Ability to work effectively, diplomatically and professionally with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. • Ability to exercise judgment in establishing and executing priorities. • Ability to understand and meet customers’ needs and expectations. • Knowledge of and confidence in event operations. • Strong time management skills with the ability to meet deadlines. • Strong detail orientation. • Ability to adhere to University & departmental policies and procedures. • Ability to work independently with minimum supervision. • Ability to maintain a neat and clean workspace. • Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and events in a fluid, changing environment. • Ability to read and comprehend simple instructions, short correspondence, memos, blue prints and schematic. Ability to write simple correspondence. Ability to effectively present information in one-on-one and small group situations to customers, clients, and other employees of the organization. • Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. Ability to compute rate, ratio, and percent and to draw and interpret graphs. • Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1071P Posting Open Date 04/22/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6486": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | TXWES Esports Digital Media Producer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us TXWES Esports Digital Media Producer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is reserved for Texas Wesleyan University Students who have work study. Posting Details Position Information Job Title TXWES Esports Digital Media Producer Position Summary The Digital Media Producer is a student position that creates photo and video content for Student Affairs. The role includes covering events, recording interviews, producing short-form content and organizing media projects from planning through final delivery. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Create photo and video content, conduct interviews, cover Student Affairs events, edit short-form media, organize digital files and manage multiple projects from planning through final delivery. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Experience Preferred experience with photography, video production, camera equipment, editing software and creating short-form digital content. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong communication, organization and time-management skills, along with proficiency in photography, video production, editing software and digital storytelling. The ideal candidate should also be dependable, professional, adaptable and able to work independently and with a team. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants This position is reserved for Texas Wesleyan University Students who have work study. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Media File Portfolio List of Three References 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6380": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Summer Resident Assistant",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Summer Resident Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Summer Resident Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Summer Resident Assistant Position Summary Residence Life is looking for students to be in the residence halls during the summer months to be able to support and be a resource to students living on-campus. You will also gain experience by assisting with various camps and facilities operations. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Attend regular one-on-one meetings with supervisor. Attend weekly staff meeting. Facilitate regular interactions and programming to support summer residents. Participate in on-call rotation. Assist with room and common space cleaning. Assist with camp and conference operations. Assist with occupancy and key management. Manage Residence Life social media accounts. Conduct room inspections prior to end of summer. 1 year living on-campus is needed for this position. Due to the constant changes to the working environment in this position, additional duties may be added or retracted from the current job description at the time the need arises. The student will be informed upon changes. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Experience Must have and maintain both a cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5. Must be a current, full-time Texas Wesleyan University student Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Outstanding interpersonal and community building skills. Strong customer service skills. Effective team member participation and leadership. Ability to resolve conflicts while being fair and consistent with students especially in discipline matters. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy ( FERPA ) regulations. Ability to demonstrate a cooperative attitude while working with a student population. Possession of organizational skills. Ability to discern student needs and respond in a caring manner. Ability to maintain composure in challenging situations or emergencies. Ability to encourage others and participate in the community. Knowledge and ability to complete given tasks and assignments thoroughly, appropriately, and in a timely manner. Ability to ask questions to help solve issues, problems, and or conflicts. Ability to Interpret and disseminate information and directives. Ability to read and comprehend instructions, short correspondence, and memos. Ability to write standard correspondence. Ability to effectively present information in one-on-one and small group situations to current and prospective students and University employees. Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. Ability to work with a rotating schedule consisting of weekends, late nights, and holidays. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What experiences do you have that prepared you for this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/5749": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Academic Advising and ASC Front Desk (Work Study or Student Assistant)",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Academic Advising and ASC Front Desk (Work Study or Student Assistant) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Academic Advising and ASC Front Desk (Work Study or Student Assistant) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Academic Advising and ASC Front Desk (Work Study or Student Assistant) Position Summary Provides assistance to professional staff and students in the Academic Success Center and Academic Advising. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Running errands on campus. Picking up and delivering mail. Data entry. Re-stocking supplies. Answering telephones. Greeting guests. Special projects assigned by staff. Proctoring tests Assisting with registration days Assist with additional duties as needed such as: Covering the front desk. Scheduling appointments. Answering phones. Organizing materials. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses None required Experience None required. Will train! Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to work independently in an efficient manner. Strong interpersonal skills. Exhibit patience and positive attitudes in the learning environment. Strong customer service skills. Ability to schedule and coordinate appointments. Demonstrated proficiency with a desktop computer as well as an integrated computer system. Demonstrated proficiency with current word processing, e-mail and spreadsheet software programs. Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters, while complying with FERPA & privacy regulations. Ability to work independently in the most efficient manner with minimum supervision. Ability to handle multiple tasks while maintaining a high attention for details. Strong organizational skills to work productively and efficiently in a high traffic office. Ability to maintain a professional appearance and office atmosphere. Ability to relate well to a diverse group of individuals. Knowledge of and the ability to support and adhere to University and office policies and procedures. Ability to read and comprehend simple instructions, short correspondence, and memos. Ability to write simple correspondence. Ability to complete the physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you qualify for work-study funds? Yes No Not sure Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
