    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6458": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Sports Information Auxiliary Student Assistant (Federal Work Study) (2 Positions)",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Sports Information Auxiliary Student Assistant (Federal Work Study) (2 Positions) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Sports Information Auxiliary Student Assistant (Federal Work Study) (2 Positions) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Sports Information Auxiliary Student Assistant (Federal Work Study) (2 Positions) Position Summary The student employee will report directly to the Sports Information Director and provide assistance in all aspects of the department. The student position works closely with department staff to promote all 23 sports through RamSports.net, and social and news media outlets, as well as assists with the management of the Texas Wesleyan Game Day experience. Essential Duties and Responsibilities •\tElectronic filing, data entry, and organizing office materials and equipment News writing. •\tAssist with post-game recaps, pre-game stories, and feature stories for all 20 of Texas Wesleyan Athletics programs. Game Day. •\tHelps with the set-up, in-game and post-game duties. •\tAssist with the management of all Texas Wesleyan Athletics social media accounts on a daily basis. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Needs at least 12 completed credit hours. Experience •\tJournalism, live streaming, and working in a sport setting are desired, but not required. •\tGraphic Design and Video Editing experience is strongly desired as well as proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud elements. •\tWorking in an office setting and/or event management and promotion, as well as social media management a plus. •\tApplicants with a willingness to learn, or experience in state programs such as DakStats and/or Stat Crew desired. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities •\tMust have a working knowledge of individual sports including, but not limited to football, basketball, baseball, softball, and volleyball. •\tAbility to write creatively and tell a compelling story. •\tAbility to manage multiple projects at one time desired. •\tAbility to be creative and critical thinking. •\tAbility to have a high-energy personality and strong work ethic. •\tProficiency with Microsoft Office 365 software including but not limited to Word, Excel, Teams, Outlook, and OneDrive. •\tKnowledge of standard and digital filing procedures. •\tWorking knowledge of mainstream social media outlets. •\tThe ability to meet deadlines, and strong attention to detail. •\tProven ability to manage multiple tasks, projects, and changing priorities. •\tStrong dependability – reliable, responsible, dependable, and fulfilling obligations. •\tAbility to work independently with little or no supervision. •\tAbility to maintain confidentiality, while complying with FERPA regulations. •\tAbility to adhere to University & departmental policies and procedures. •\tAbility to attend events as scheduled. •\tAbility to work evenings and weekends. •\tAbility to complete all physical tasks and duties. •\tAbility to withstand exposure to outside weather conditions. •\tAbility to stand for extended periods of time and climb stadium stairs. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 08/03/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently enrolled as a student at Texas Wesleyan University? Yes No Do you qualify for Federal work study? yes no Are you available to work rotating shifts including days, nights, weekends and holiday? Yes No Please select your current grade level. Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6346": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Financial Aid Advisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Financial Aid Advisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Be sure to complete the University's Employment Application, provide a resume' and three references Posting Details Position Information Job Title Financial Aid Advisor Position Summary The Financial Aid Advisor is responsible for advising students, parents, and campus partners on the application, eligibility, and administration of federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs. This role reviews and evaluates financial aid applications for accuracy, completeness, and financial need using federal methodology, performs required verification and follow-up actions, and ensures compliance with all applicable federal and state regulations. Advisors must access and maintain data within federal systems, correct application information as needed, determine eligibility levels, and apply or adjust aid awards accurately within the university’s information system. In addition, the Financial Aid Advisor provides individualized and group counseling on financial aid processes, deadlines, rights and responsibilities, appeals, and eligibility decisions. The position may include specialized administrative responsibilities such as Pell Grant processing, Texas Education Grant administration, veterans’ benefits, satisfactory academic progress appeals, or Return of Title IV aid calculations. Advisors are expected to stay current on regulatory changes, support continuous improvement of forms and procedures, communicate updates to staff, and assist with outreach and presentations to students and families. The role requires a high level of professionalism, regulatory precision, and commitment to student service in a compliance-driven environment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities - Advising students, staff, and peers about how to apply for Federal Student Aid. – Financial Aid Advisors must be able to follow Federal and State regulations. - Applicant cannot be in Default on any Federal Student Loans. - This position requires staff to have access to Federal databases. - Reviews and evaluates financial aid applications to determine accuracy, completeness and financial need level. - Uses federal methodology need analysis criteria for review. - Performs any required follow-up procedures to get additional information, correct errors or elicit more in-depth data from applicants. - Performs verifications. - Compares FAFSA data with verification documents (1040’s, Worksheets, W-2s, etc.). – Corrects information on data base, performs needs analysis, and prepares computer files for reprocessing. - Evaluates satisfactory academic progress student suspension appeals and determines future aid eligibility based on appeal results. - Applies financial aid awards in the computer system. Determines need levels, confirms resources and awards funds within parameters. Uses computer to automatically “package” available aid, or manually inputs awards on an individual student by student basis. - Provides one-on-one or small group counseling for students, parents or others regarding financial aid issues, procedures to award, reasons for denial or lack of eligibility, deadlines, petition processes and other relevant issues. - May perform tuition refund/repayment calculations according to return of Title IV aid guidelines. Determines amounts of aid that must be refunded to a federal program and amounts student must repay. - Conducts presentations of FAFSA application procedures, aid eligibility and availability, rights and responsibilities to groups of high school seniors, parents and current students, either on campus or at local schools. - May have specific aid program administrative responsibilities such as the Texas Education Grant ( TEG ), Pell payment and reconciliation, Veteran’s assistance, or return of Title IV aid. Stays current with Federal and State regulations and procedures. - Informs staff of pertaining regulatory and procedural changes as they occur. - Ensures that forms and processes are current. Makes recommendations about forms that need revision in accordance with federally required documentation. - Other duties as assigned by The Director of Financial Aid or Assistant Director of Financial Aid. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and two years of relevant work experience Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and five years of relevant work experience. Additional education may be substituted for work experience. Experience Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of relevant work experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of relevant work experience. Additional education may be substituted for work experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities - Considerable knowledge of financial aid policies, procedures and operations. - Knowledge of federal and state regulations, policies and procedures relating to awarding and administering financial aid. – Knowledge and skill with networked financial aid computer system and Colleague software. - Skills with and knowledge of applicable word processing and spread sheet applications. - Ability to independently perform all of the duties of the position with efficiency, effectiveness and in strict confidence. - Ability to analyze technical and complex information and documents and make assessments according to well established policies, procedures and mandated regulations. - Ability to impart technical and detailed information through one-on-one or group presentations. - Ability to perform data entry and database management duties and other general record keeping and file maintenance duties. - Ability to communicate both formally and informally with a wide range of contacts both inside and outside the university setting. - Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. - Ability to be discrete handling confidential matters, while complying with FERPA and privacy regulations. - Reliable judgment, trusted discretion, strong interpersonal skills to relate to numerous and varied constituencies of the university. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1026P Posting Open Date 04/24/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Be sure to complete the University’s Employment Application, provide a resume’ and three references Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * Do you have working knowledge of Ellucian Colleague? Yes No Have you been the lead of any program within the Financial Aid Office? If Yes, what program did you lead? (Open Ended Question) * How many years of working experience do you have that includes a working knowledge of financial aid, insurance principles, practices and law? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation List of Three References Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/5819": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | 2025-2026 Resident Assistant",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | 2025-2026 Resident Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us 2025-2026 Resident Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title 2025-2026 Resident Assistant Position Summary The Resident Assistant (RA) plays a vital role in fostering a supportive and inclusive living environment within the university residence halls. This position involves serving as a resource, mentor, and leader for a designated group of students within the residential community. RAs are responsible for building relationships, promoting community engagement, and ensuring the safety and well-being of residents. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Building Community: Foster a sense of belonging and community among residents through organized activities, events, and programming. Mentorship and Support: Serve as a resource and mentor for residents, offering guidance, advice, and support in academic, personal, and social matters. Conflict Resolution: Address conflicts and concerns within the residence hall, mediating disputes and facilitating open communication among residents. Policy Enforcement: Enforce university policies and regulations within the residence hall, including those related to safety, conduct, and community standards. Emergency Response: Respond promptly to emergencies and crises within the residence hall, following established protocols and procedures. Administrative Duties: Complete administrative tasks such as documenting incidents, maintaining records, and submitting reports as required. On-Call Responsibilities: Participate in on-call rotations to provide after-hours support and assistance to residents as needed. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Experience Must have and maintain both a cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5 Must be a current, full-time Texas Wesleyan University student Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Outstanding interpersonal and community building skills. Strong customer service skills. Effective team member participation and leadership. Ability to resolve conflicts while being fair and consistent with students especially in discipline matters. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy ( FERPA ) regulations. Ability to demonstrate a cooperative attitude while working with a diverse student population. Possession of organizational skills. Ability to discern student needs and respond in a caring manner. Ability to maintain composure in challenging situations or emergencies. Ability to encourage others and participate in the community. Knowledge and ability to complete given tasks and assignments thoroughly, appropriately, and in a timely manner. Ability to ask questions to help solve issues, problems, and or conflicts. Ability to Interpret and disseminate information and directives. Ability to promote and execute inclusion and diversification within the residential halls and campus community. Ability to read and comprehend instructions, short correspondence, and memos. Ability to write standard correspondence. Ability to effectively present information in one-on-one and small group situations to current and prospective students and University employees. Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. Ability to work with a rotating schedule consisting of weekends, late nights, and holidays. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please provide your definition of integrity and how you would apply that to the RA role. (Open Ended Question) Based on your experience and skills, what population of students do you think would benefit most from you as an RA and why? (i.e. first year, transfer, international, upperclassmen, student athlete, etc.) (Open Ended Question) Please provide a detailed program idea that would best help develop community within your floor/residence hall. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6491": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Lead New Student Mentor (2026-2027) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Lead New Student Mentor (2026-2027) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If you would like assistance with your resume, cover letter, or other application materials, please contact Career Services at careerservices@txwes.edu. Application will remain open until filled, however, Priority Deadline for Consideration: Sept. 18. 2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title Lead New Student Mentor (2026-2027) Position Summary The Lead New Student Mentor works as a member of the TXWES Orientation team and serves in an advanced peer-leadership role that helps further the mission and focus of the Division of Student Affairs. This position helps lead and mentor a team of New Student Mentors while assisting with the planning, development, and facilitation of New Student Registration Days, Ram Camp, and related Orientation and Transition Programs. The Lead New Student Mentor gains experience working across multiple areas of the division, develops short- and long-term programmatic goals, and helps incoming students transition successfully to Texas Wesleyan University through positive, professional, and welcoming service. The position also helps the student employee build advanced leadership, project management, and mentorship skills while supporting the university’s mission of student success. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Build relationships with new students to support their transition to Texas Wesleyan University, serving as an approachable, positive, and reliable point of contact throughout the orientation process. Lead and support a team of New Student Mentors by providing guidance, mentorship, and day-to-day direction throughout the orientation season. Lead a small group of new students throughout their orientation experience, guiding them through Ram Camp and New Student Registration Days activities and helping them build connections with peers. Assist in the maintenance and development of departmental projects, including Ram Camp programming, Registration Days logistics, the parent newsletter, social media content, and attendee spreadsheets. Attend and actively participate in all required trainings during the semester and summer, and all Orientation dates, including Ram Camp and mid-year and summer New Student Registration Days. Work with fellow New Student Mentors and Orientation staff to plan, coordinate, and carry out welcome weekend activities that help incoming students feel supported and included. Encourage and support students, student organizations, academic departments, and campus programs by promoting events and initiatives that benefit the student community and align with the university’s mission, and cultivate positive working relationships with staff, faculty, and students. Adhere to all university and departmental policies and guidelines, complete other assigned duties, and protect confidential student information in accordance with FERPA . Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Must be enrolled as a student in good standing at Texas Wesleyan University, maintain a minimum semester GPA of 2.0 & cumulative GPA of 2.5 throughout the completion of the contract, and maintain eligibility for student employment in accordance with university policies. Ability to attend all mandatory trainings, New Student Registration Days, and Ram Camp sessions throughout the summer and academic year. Experience Demonstrated experience in orientation, student leadership, event planning, or involvement in student organizations. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Excellent written, oral, social media-based, and interpersonal communication skills Ability to discern student needs and respond in a caring, supportive manner Ability to articulate enthusiasm and support for all students within the campus community Outstanding interpersonal and community-building skills Ability to assess student and team needs during orientation and respond using sound judgment Knowledge and ability to complete assigned tasks thoroughly, appropriately, and in a timely manner Ability to be creative and bring new ideas and energy to the position Possession of strong organizational skills Ability to lead, mentor, and instruct a team of New Student Mentors. Demonstrated experience in, or aptitude for, orientation, student leadership, and event planning encouraged Ability to encourage others and actively participate in the campus community Models a positive, high-energy, and welcoming approach to New Student Programs and Orientation Ability to be discreet in handling confidential matters while complying with FERPA regulations Ability to adhere to all university and departmental policies and procedures Maintains reliability, accountability, and a strong work ethic Ability to attend all mandatory meetings and trainings Ability to work independently and in a team setting in an efficient manner. Ability to demonstrate a cooperative attitude while collaborating with a diverse student population Cultivates and maintains good working relationships with staff, faculty, and fellow mentors Ability to articulate passion and support for all students, honoring the diverse backgrounds and experiences represented within the student community Basic knowledge of Outlook, Word, and Excel Ability to communicate effectively using social media and digital platforms, including managing social media content for departmental projects Ability to learn and utilize university systems and technology to support Orientation programming Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 08/20/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date 09/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants If you would like assistance with your resume, cover letter, or other application materials, please contact Career Services at careerservices@txwes.edu. Application will remain open until filled, however, Priority Deadline for Consideration: Sept. 18. 2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your overall GPA? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a 2.5 cumulative grade point average or higher? Yes No * Do you qualify for work-study funds? Yes No Not sure * Please explain your previous involvement with TXWES Orientation and years served. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) List of Three References Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6382": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Athlete Academic Support and Retention Student Assistant",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Athlete Academic Support and Retention Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Athlete Academic Support and Retention Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Athlete Academic Support and Retention Student Assistant Position Summary The Texas Wesleyan University Athletic Department is looking for a student employee who will assist in various activities for the academic support and well-being of our student-athletes. The student will work various hours depending on needs of the department and time of year. Essential Duties and Responsibilities • Monitor and record attendance for student-athlete study sessions; ensure a quiet, productive environment conducive to learning. • Meet with student-athletes to provide peer academic support, time management strategies, and encouragement as needed. • Help plan, coordinate, and execute academic workshops, recognition events, and other department-sponsored programs. • Assist the Assistant Athletic Director for Academic Services and Retention with social media, clerical tasks, scheduling, data entry, and preparing materials for meetings or events. • Maintain strict adherence to institutional and federal privacy laws (e.g., FERPA ) regarding student records and information. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Experience None required, training will be given Knowledge, Skills & Abilities • Currently enrolled undergraduate or graduate student in good standing (minimum sophomore standing) • Minimum cumulative GPA of 3.25 (3.5 preferred) • Strong interpersonal, written and oral communication skills • Professionalism, reliability, and attention to detail • Ability to work independently and as part of a team • Commitment to upholding confidentiality and privacy standards • Interest in academic support, student success, or student-athlete development • Ability to work effectively, diplomatically and professionally with a wide range of constituencies. • Ability to exercise judgment in establishing and executing priorities. • Ability to understand and meet customers, coaches, and staff needs and expectations. • Strong time management skills with the ability to meet deadlines. • Ability to adhere to University & departmental policies and procedures. • Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and events in a fluid, changing environment. • Ability to react calmly and effectively in emergency situations. • Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. • Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form. • Ability to complete all physical tasks and duties. • Ability to move around campus running errands. • Ability to withstand exposure to outside weather conditions. • Prior experience as a student-athlete or in a student support/service role (preferred) • Knowledge of NAIA rules and regulations related to academic eligibility (a plus, but not required) Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Letter of Recommendation Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/5667": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Supplemental Instruction Leader Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Supplemental Instruction Leader Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Supplemental Instruction Leader Position Summary Under the direction of the campus-based Supplemental Instruction Supervisor, this position facilitates student learning and helps students better understand concepts or applications of course content for a variety of courses. 8 hours a week maximum for 16 weeks only. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Meets with Supervisor as needed to plan, implement, and assess assigned plan of work. Completes and submits supplemental instruction study session plans to Supervisor. Attends and/or watches all class meetings of target course. Takes accurate notes, and understands all homework/reading assignments and projects. Facilitates weekly one-hour supplemental instruction sessions. Maintains one office hour per week. Confers with Supervisor two to four times per month. Attends and participates in all supplemental leader training and group meetings as required. Attends the workplace regularly, reports to work punctually and follows a work schedule to keep up with the demands of the worksite. Attend SI Leader training workshop prior to the beginning of each term. Make periodic announcements about the availability of the SI sessions to the students. Collect attendance data for every SI session, including student names, course title, date, and time of session. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Have a class schedule that permits them to attend (or review material from) the class for which they are SI Leader, as well as hold at least one Supplemental Instruction session per week. Faculty recommendation for content competency. Have a GPA of 3.0 or above in their major. Experience Have completed the course for which they will be Supplemental Instruction Leader. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge Knowledge of: The content area for which they will be Supplementary Instruction Leader. Skills and abilities Skill in: Accessing classroom information through the Blackboard Learning Management System. Ability to work with a diverse student population. Strong time management and organizational skills. Effective interpersonal and communication skills. Strong organizational skills to work productively. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy ( FERPA ) regulations. Ability to maintain a working schedule for instruction and meetings with supervisor. Ability to be punctual to trainings and meetings. Ability and knowledge to lead instructional sessions. Ability and working knowledge to take questions from students and answer in a professional manner. Demonstrate knowledge and competence in the subject matter. Enjoy tutoring the subject for which services are being provided. Effectively communicate study strategies to ensure academic success. Ability to instruct others. Ability to maintain a neat & professional appearance and office atmosphere. Ability to read and comprehend instructions, standard correspondence, and memos. Ability to write simple correspondence. Ability to complete job tasks and assignments thoroughly, appropriately, and in a timely manner. Good interpersonal and communication skills are required. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 07/22/2024 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your overall GPA? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
