    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/5716": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | School of Business Administration Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us School of Business Administration Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title School of Business Administration Position Summary Student employee will provide support for the School of Business Administration ( SOBA ). Duties include clerical and receptionist responsibilities. Will assist administrative personnel and professors with various clerical duties and SOBA events. Federal Work-Study Awarded students preferred. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Support SOBA staff including front office responsibilities, special events and programs, scanning, filing, running errands and sorting mail. Answer telephone calls and transfer the calls to appropriate individual or department. Maintain a clean, organized and professional work environment. Assist students, faculty, staff and visitors with excellent customer services. Communicate and resume any tasks that were not completed during the previous shift. Assist with SOBA events set up and tear down. Assist lab users with basic computer programs. Monitor computer usage and maintain an accurate log. Restock copiers with paper and other supplies as needed. Notify the office staff of any faulty or defective computer equipment. Enforce the no food or drink policy in the computer labs. Arrange desks, chairs and computer equipment at the end of the shift/day in preparation for the next shift. Due to the nature of the position, other duties and responsibilities may be needed. Students will be informed of any changes. Preferably looking for Federal Work-Study awarded students. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses High school diploma or general education degree ( GED ) required. Experience None required, will train! Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to work well with diverse faculty, staff, and students. Ability to work independently in an efficient and effective manner with minimum supervision. Ability to follow instructions or directives and promptly complete tasks as requested without follow-up. Ability to handle a variety of responsibilities and multitask on a short notice. Ability to maintain confidentiality, while complying with FERPA regulations. Ability to work during the day and periodic evening events during Fall and Spring semesters. Proficiency with an integrated administrative system and current software programs (MS Office), especially Word and Excel. Proficient use of standard office equipment. Ability to adhere to university and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to work effectively and cooperatively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Ability to maintain composure in difficult situations. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled No Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you qualify for work-study funds? Yes No Not sure Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Transcripts Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6467": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Library Circulation Student Assistant - Friday and Saturday",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Library Circulation Student Assistant - Friday and Saturday Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Library Circulation Student Assistant - Friday and Saturday Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Library Circulation Student Assistant - Friday and Saturday Position Summary This position is required to work: Friday 7:30am to 5pm Saturday 11am to 5pm. -Provide clerical and receptionist support for the West library. -Provide outstanding customer service. -Process incoming and outgoing materials. -Provide basic computer and copier assistance. -Shelving of books and materials. -Inventory books and materials to maintain good order of the stacks. -Cleaning throughout the library. Essential Duties and Responsibilities -Must be detail-oriented and be able to follow verbal and written instructions. -Perform special projects and other duties as assigned. -Excellent oral and written communication skills. -Must be proactive and able to engage with a diverse constituency. -Demonstrate decision-making and problem-solving skills. -Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned Education, Certifications and/or Licenses - High school diploma or general education degree ( GED ) required - Some college preferred Experience - Computer experience - Experience in a higher education setting preferred Knowledge, Skills & Abilities -Knowledge of Microsoft Office -Knowledge of standard office practices and procedures, including filing Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently enrolled as a student at Texas Wesleyan University? Yes No Are you a current employee of the university? Yes No Have you worked in an academic library before? Yes No Have you ever worked on Campus before? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6126": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Summer Facilities Assistant",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Summer Facilities Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Summer Facilities Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Summer Facilities Assistant Position Summary The Summer Facilities Crew is responsible for ensuring residence hall rooms are in move-in condition for summer operations, for the completion of facilities related projects in the residence halls, for the upkeep and maintenance of the residence halls throughout the summer months and for setting up and breaking down rooms. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Prepare rooms for the summer in the Residence Halls. Prepare all guest rooms in a timely and organized manner. Conduct room inspections prior to guest arrival and after departure. Assist with light cleaning sweeps (i.e. taking out trash, wiping down counters) for camp and conference rooms. Perform lounge checks on a regular basis to ensure clean and comfortable spaces for guests. Assist with key checks throughout buildings previously occupied. Occasionally assist with large weekend check-ins. Occasionally assist with key/combo preparation or audits. Receive and document all Residence Life deliveries. Manage Summer Housing storage spaces on campus. Inspections of Residence Halls: Inspection of residence halls and surrounding grounds area, and entry of work orders as needed. Work closely with a variety of departments to successfully execute summer operations. Must be a current, full-time Texas Wesleyan University student. Due to the constant changes to the working environment in this position, additional duties may be added or retracted from the current job description at the time the need arises. The student will be informed upon changes. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Experience Must have and maintain both a cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5 Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Outstanding interpersonal and community building skills. Strong customer service skills. Effective team member participation and leadership. Ability to encourage others and participate in the community. Knowledge and ability to complete given tasks and assignments thoroughly, appropriately, and in a timely manner. Ability to work with a rotating schedule consisting of weekends, late nights, and holidays. Must be able to take direction from the Facilities Crew Supervisor Must have the ability to work well with others in a fast paced environment. Must have the ability to safely lift up to 50 pounds. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 02/02/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What experiences do you have that prepared you for this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6434": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Admissions Transcript Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Admissions Transcript Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Admissions Transcript Analyst Position Summary The Admissions Transcript Analyst is responsible for the accurate intake, evaluation, and processing of academic transcripts and application records for domestic students. This role is central to the operational integrity of the admissions pipeline — ensuring that incoming documents are matched correctly, application data is reviewed for accuracy, and discrepancies are identified and routed appropriately. The Analyst works closely with the Assistant Director of Admissions Operations, admissions counselors, and the Office of the Registrar to support a complete and compliant admissions record for each applicant. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Receive, log, and match incoming transcripts and academic documents to applicant records in Slate; identify and resolve document exceptions including mismatched records, incomplete submissions, and routing errors; monitor intake workflows and flag recurring issues or process friction points to the Assistant Director. Review application records for data accuracy and internal consistency, identifying discrepancies that may affect applicant classification, eligibility, or downstream processing; route flagged issues to the appropriate staff member with clear documentation and recommended action; apply knowledge of admissions classifications to evaluate whether records require reclassification or additional materials. Evaluate domestic academic transcripts for accuracy, authenticity, and compliance with Texas Wesleyan’s admissions requirements; conduct GPA conversion and verification and assess coursework equivalencies; enter and update transcript evaluations in Slate; communicate with school counselors regarding submission issues, clarifications, corrections, and missing information. Conduct regular audits of applicant records to identify and resolve duplicate records, data entry errors, and inconsistencies across systems; maintain accurate and up-to-date academic records in coordination with the Assistant Director and the Office of the Registrar; flag systemic issues and contribute to ongoing process improvement. Work within Slate CRM to manage transcript data, process records, and support reporting functions; assist the Assistant Director in identifying opportunities to reduce manual tracking and streamline data workflows; generate reports related to transcript processing and application review as needed. Collaborate with admissions counselors, the Office of the Registrar, and other campus partners to ensure a complete and accurate admissions record for each applicant; ensure all activities comply with university policies and FERPA regulations; contribute to documentation of operational procedures and support cross-training efforts. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Bachelor’s degree required. Experience Experience in admissions processing, academic records, transcript evaluation, or a closely related field preferred. Experience working with Slate CRM or a comparable student information system preferred. Familiarity with Ellucian Colleague or similar ERP systems a plus. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of admissions classifications, applicant types, and enrollment policies as they relate to record processing. Knowledge of FERPA regulations and confidentiality requirements governing academic records. Familiarity with transcript evaluation standards, GPA conversion, and accreditation considerations for domestic institutions. Skill in: •Strong analytical and critical thinking skills, with demonstrated ability to identify inconsistencies and exercise judgment in ambiguous situations. •High degree of accuracy and attention to detail, particularly in data entry and record review. •Strong organizational skills and ability to manage a high-volume workload with competing priorities and deadlines. •Effective written and verbal communication skills for interacting with counselors, staff, and campus partners. •Ability to apply institutional policies and admissions classifications to real records and recognize when exceptions require escalation. •Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and in full compliance with FERPA regulations. •Proficiency with Microsoft Office and database or CRM platforms; Slate experience strongly preferred. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1121P Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6372": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool - Honors Program - General University",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool - Honors Program - General University Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Adjunct Instructor Pool - Honors Program - General University Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Instructor Pool - Honors Program - General University Position Summary Designs and delivers instruction in primarily undergraduate courses offered by the Honors (Wesleyan Scholars) Program. Participates in all department, various schools, and University-wide tasks and activities. Disciplines include: • Art • Biology • Chemistry • Cultural Studies • English • Ethnic Studies • History • Mass Communications • Music (History/Theory/Applied) • Political Science • Psychology • Religion • Sociology • Theater Essential Duties and Responsibilities • Prepares lessons and delivers instruction primarily for undergraduate courses. • Adheres to the faculty handbook and faculty guide. Meets classes for the required time and days in accordance with polices established for class schedule. Holds required office hours, keeps attendance, submits contracts, book requests, syllabi, grades, evaluations, and other required paperwork and reports in a timely manner. • Remains knowledgeable of current research activities in respective discipline by reading journal articles, attending conferences, and maintaining relationships with other fellow researchers. • Participates in curriculum assessment. • Other duties as assigned by the Honors Director Education, Certifications and/or Licenses • Masters degree, with a minimum of 18 hours in the discipline being taught.. Experience • Preferred, prior teaching experience at the college or university level preferred with evidence of teaching excellence. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities • Ability to work effectively with other University personnel. • Ability to provide service to both the University and the community. • Ability to comply with rules, standards, regulations and laws related to student records. • Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. • Ability to use discretion in handling confidential and sensitive matters. • Ability to read, analyze, and interpret standard periodicals, professional journals, and/or governmental regulations. • Ability to write reports, academic correspondence, and procedure manuals. • Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, students, and University employees. • Ability to calculate figures & amounts such as discounts, interest, commissions, proportions, percentages, area, & volume. • Ability to apply concepts of basic algebra, geometry, calculus and statistics. • Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. • Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS880P Posting Open Date 01/01/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the discipline(s) that you are interested in applying for.  NOTE:  You must have transcripts verifying at least 18 hours of coursework in the discipline being taught. Communications Liberal Studies Humanities Theatre Music (History/Theory) Music (Applied) English French Spanish Religion (Christian Studies) Religion (Comparative Studies) * Please select the discipline(s) that you are interested in applying for.  NOTE:  You must have transcripts verifying at least 18 hours of coursework in the discipline being taught. Biology Chemistry/Biochemistry Computer Science Criminal Justice History Mathematics Paralegal Studies Political Science Psychology Sociology Computer Information Systems * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No * Are you available to work weekends? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Do you live or plan on working outside the state of Texas? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) Letter of Recommendation 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
