    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6470": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Student Social Media and Marketing Assistant",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Student Social Media and Marketing Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Student Social Media and Marketing Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Student Social Media and Marketing Assistant Position Summary The Student Social Media and Marketing Assistant is a part-time student worker position that supports the Graduate Programs of Nurse Anesthesia ( GPNA ) through content creation, social media engagement, event promotion, and marketing initiatives. Working under the supervision of GPNA faculty and staff, the student assistant will help showcase student experiences, program achievements, simulation activities, community outreach, and special events. This position provides valuable hands-on experience in healthcare marketing, communications, social media management, photography, videography, and event promotion while contributing to the visibility and success of one of the nation’s largest nurse anesthesia programs. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Social Media Support ·      Assist with maintaining GPNA social media accounts, including Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, and other platforms. ·      Create and schedule posts highlighting student activities, faculty accomplishments, simulation events, graduations, and program milestones. ·      Assist with developing engaging content including photos, videos, graphics, and short-form social media content. ·      Monitor social media engagement and provide recommendations for increasing audience reach and participation. Content Creation ·      Capture photographs and videos during GPNA events, simulation labs, workshops, and ceremonies. ·      Design promotional graphics using Canva or similar design platforms. ·      Assist in creating newsletters, announcements, and digital marketing materials. ·      Collect student and alumni stories that showcase program success and professional achievements. Event Promotion and Support ·      Assist faculty and staff with marketing and promotion of: o GPNA Open House events o   Simulation Symposium o   Graduation ceremonies o   Student organization activities o   Recruitment events o   Alumni engagement activities ·      Provide event-day support including photography, social media updates, and attendee engagement. Website and Communications Support ·      Assist with maintaining current content on GPNA webpages and digital communication platforms. ·      Help organize photo and video archives for future marketing use. ·      Support communication efforts with prospective students, alumni, and program stakeholders Education, Certifications and/or Licenses ·      Major or minor in Marketing, Communications, Journalism, Public Relations, Graphic Design, Digital Media, or related field. Experience ·      Current undergraduate student in good academic standing. ·      Strong written and verbal communication skills. ·      Familiarity with major social media platforms. ·      Basic experience with Canva, Adobe Express, or similar graphic design software. ·      Ability to work independently and meet deadlines. ·      Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. ·      Experience managing social media accounts. ·      Experience with photography, videography, or video editing. ·      Interest in healthcare, nursing, or higher education marketing. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities ·      Creativity and enthusiasm for storytelling through digital media. ·      Professional communication skills. ·      Ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism. ·      Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students. ·      Willingness to learn new marketing and communication strategies. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 08/10/2026 Open Until Filled Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) List of Three References Optional Documents Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6439": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Graduate Student Assistant",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Graduate Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Graduate Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Must be currently enrolled in the Marriage and Family Therapy PhD program at Texas Wesleyan University Must hold a Full or Associate license required (LPC/A, LMFT/A) Posting Details Position Information Job Title Graduate Student Assistant Position Summary The Graduate Student Assistant at the Texas Wesleyan University Community Counseling Center ( TWUCCC ) provides administrative, operational, and client support to ensure the efficient and professional functioning of the counseling center. This role is essential in maintaining clinic workflow, supporting student therapists, and upholding ethical, confidentiality, and documentation standards consistent with training clinic expectations. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Key Responsibilities and Duties: Front Desk & Client Support Greet and assist clients in a professional and welcoming manner Answer phone calls, respond to general inquiries, and direct calls appropriately Support client check-in and check-out procedures Maintain a calm and organized front office environment Scheduling & Systems Support Assist with appointment scheduling and coordination using the center’s electronic health record system (e.g., TheraNest/Ensora) Monitor student therapists schedules and notify leadership of discrepancies (e.g., missing room assignments, scheduling conflicts) Support room reservations and ensure accurate scheduling of counseling spaces Documentation & Records Management Assist in ensuring client files are complete, including demographic and required intake information Scan, upload, and organize documents in accordance with center policies Maintain accurate and timely record-keeping while adhering to confidentiality standards Operational & Administrative Support Support daily clinic operations, including supply management and organization of shared spaces Maintain logs (e.g., cash payment logs) and assist with administrative tracking systems Assist leadership with data entry, reports, and special projects as assigned Walk-In Student Crisis Support Immediately notify clinical leadership when a walk-in student presents in crisis Assist with coordinating communication between student therapists and clinical leadership Assist and see crisis walk- in students in the event that no student therapist available (Full or Associate license required) Help maintain a calm and structured environment in the waiting area during walk-in student crisis situations Support leadership by assisting with logistics (e.g., room availability, client flow) Follow all center protocols while maintaining clear boundaries Student & Clinical Support Provide general support to student therapist while maintaining appropriate role boundaries Assist with clinic flow to ensure sessions begin and end on time Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Must be currently enrolled in the Marriage and Family Therapy PhD program at Texas Wesleyan University Must hold a Full or Associate license required ( LPC /A, LMFT /A) Experience None needed -just an eagerness to learn Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Would like: Knowledge of TheraNest (Ensora) Knowledge of how a community counseling center works (administration support) Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 06/30/2026 Open Until Filled Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Must be currently enrolled in the Marriage and Family Therapy PhD program at Texas Wesleyan University Must hold a Full or Associate license required ( LPC /A, LMFT /A) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Cover Letter 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6233": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool - Graduate Counseling Program",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool - Graduate Counseling Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Adjunct Instructor Pool - Graduate Counseling Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position must be applied for once you are asked to teach a course in the Graduate Counseling Programs. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Instructor Pool - Graduate Counseling Program Position Summary Designs and delivers instruction in primarily graduate courses offered by the School of Health Professions. Programs include the Masters of Science in Marriage and Family Therapy, Masters of Arts in Licensed Professional Counseling, the Certified School Counselor and the PhD in Marriage and Family Therapy. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Adheres to the faculty handbook and faculty guide. Meets classes for the required time and days in accordance with polices established for class schedule. Submits contracts, book requests, syllabi, grades, evaluations, and other required paperwork and reports in a timely manner. Remains knowledgeable of current research activities in respective discipline by reading journal articles, attending conferences, and maintaining relationships with other fellow researchers. Other duties as assigned by the Dean or Department Chair Education, Certifications and/or Licenses PhD or PhD-C in a field of Counseling that is related to the graduate course assigned. For example, a PhD in Marriage and Family Therapy for a MFT course. Must be licensed as a LPC , LMFT or Certified School Counselor in the State of Texas, in relevance to the graduate course assigned. Experience Prior teaching experience at the college or university level preferred with evidence of teaching excellence. Ability to work effectively with other University personnel. Ability to comply with rules, standards, regulations and laws related to student records. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to use discretion in handling confidential and sensitive matters. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities LANGUAGE SKILLS Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general counseling periodicals, professional journals, and/or governmental regulations. MATHEMATICAL SKILLS Ability to calculate figures & amounts such as percentages. Ability to apply concepts of basic statistics. REASONING ABILITY Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form. CONFIDENTIALITY Ability to keep confidential any client history or file that may be disclosed in practicum class per student discussion. ETHICAL KNOWLEDGE - Knowledge of appropriate professional ethics code for the course taught such as ACA , AAMFT or ASCA . HYBRID TRAINING - Must be open to receiving training from CETL , the University Center for online teaching hybrid and online courses for all courses taught in this manner. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS892P Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants This position must be applied for once you are asked to teach a course in the Graduate Counseling Programs. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Transcripts Optional Documents Cover Letter Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) Curriculum Vitae 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
