    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/5727": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | ASC FIN1325 Tutor (Work Study or Student Assistant)",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | ASC FIN1325 Tutor (Work Study or Student Assistant) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us ASC FIN1325 Tutor (Work Study or Student Assistant) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title ASC FIN1325 Tutor (Work Study or Student Assistant) Position Summary Provides academic tutoring services to students on an individual basis or in small groups. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide academic tutoring services by maintaining a weekly schedule of available hours for appointments. Attend tutor training workshops as required. Keep accurate records of tutoring appointments by filing tutoring reports. Maintain contact with professors in your subject of expertise in order to obtain pertinent materials for the ASC . Assist undergraduate students with assignments. Tutoring appointments are intended to assists students in becoming better students. Assist with additional duties as needed such as, covering the front desk, scheduling tutoring appointments, answering phones, organizing materials and maintaining information in the ASC . Education, Certifications and/or Licenses High school diploma/ GED required. Successfully completed courses in subject area tutoring with a grade of “A” or “B” at Texas Wesleyan (exceptions upon discretion of the Director). Successfully demonstrate skills in subject by scoring the minimum required score on grammar and proofing test. Minimum GPA of 3.0 (exceptions upon discretion of the Director). Experience Formal or informal tutoring experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters pertaining to student’s privacy. Ability to work independently in an efficient manner. Ability to instruct others. Strong interpersonal skills. Demonstrate knowledge and competence in the subject matter. Enjoy tutoring the subject for which services are being provided. Effectively communicate study strategies to ensure academic success. Work comfortably with people from various backgrounds. Exhibit patience and positive attitudes in the learning environment. Ability to provide and demonstrate quality customer service. Pleasant and clearly understandable phone voice. Strong organizational skills to work productively. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy ( FERPA ) regulations. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you eligible for Work Study? Yes No * Have you completed the course you want to tutor at Texas Wesleyan with an A or B? No Yes Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Transcripts Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6477": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Career Services Student Assistant (Work-Study &amp; Non-Work-Study)",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Career Services Student Assistant (Work-Study &amp; Non-Work-Study) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Career Services Student Assistant (Work-Study & Non-Work-Study) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Career Services Student Assistant (Work-Study & Non-Work-Study) Position Summary The Office of Career Services Student Assistant provides administrative, customer service, and event support to help students and alumni with career exploration, resume and interview preparation, internship and employment opportunities, and career readiness programming. This position helps the student employee strengthen transferable workplace skills, build professionalism and leadership experience, and support the Career Services Center’s mission of preparing students for successful career outcomes after graduation. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Communicate professionally with students, alumni, employers, faculty, staff, and visitors in person, by phone, and through email to answer questions, take accurate messages, and provide assistance. | Daily 25% | Use Handshake to help schedule appointments, manage student requests, approve job postings from verified employers, and support office communications. | Daily 25% | Provide organized and accurate administrative support, including filing, organizing materials, maintaining office spaces, entering data, and supporting daily operations. | Daily 15% | Assist with survey administration, outreach, and accurate data collection for the First Destination Survey during the fall and spring semesters. | As needed 10% | Work with the Career Services team to support campus recruiting and employer events by setting up welcome and registration tables, greeting guests, managing sign-ins, and assisting with event logistics. | As needed 10% | Represent the Office of Career Services professionally at Orientation programs, Welcome Stations, tabling events, and employer-facing initiatives. | As needed 5% | Support the team in preparing and carrying out large-scale Career Services events, including Career Fairs, employer programs, and related activities. | Monthly 5% | Provide limited front-line Housing support as needed by monitoring the Housing phone and email, answering basic questions, and referring other concerns to Housing staff. Complete other assigned duties while protecting confidential information and following university policies. | As needed 5% | Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Experience Required Must be pursuing a bachelor’s degree at Texas Wesleyan University and maintain eligibility for student employment in accordance with university policies. Preferred Previous customer service, office, leadership, or campus involvement experience. Training Career Services systems, Handshake, office procedures, event support, and basic Housing phone and email coverage and referral procedures. Students are not expected to know these department-specific systems or procedures before starting. Expectations Participate in training, apply feedback, ask questions, and continue developing communication, teamwork, professionalism, leadership, critical thinking, technology, and career and self-development skills. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Career & Self-Development: Demonstrates initiative by seeking opportunities to learn Career Services programs, resources, and office procedures Ability to manage multiple tasks, deadlines, and responsibilities effectively Shows adaptability when responding to changing office, event, and student needs Takes ownership of assigned tasks, applies feedback, and follows through independently Communication: Ability to communicate clearly and professionally with students, alumni, employers, faculty, staff, and visitors Strong verbal and written communication skills for phone, email, and in-person interactions Ability to explain Career Services resources, appointment processes, and basic office information accurately Demonstrates active listening and refers questions or concerns to the appropriate staff member when needed Critical Thinking: Ability to identify student and visitor needs and respond using sound judgment Uses established procedures to solve routine problems and determine when assistance is needed Strong attention to detail when supporting Handshake, First Destination Survey outreach, and office projects Ability to prioritize responsibilities and adjust to changing departmental needs Leadership: Demonstrates initiative in supporting office operations, events, outreach, and special projects Ability to take ownership of assigned responsibilities and complete tasks with minimal supervision Contributes ideas that improve student service, office processes, and event support Models a welcoming, dependable, and student-focused approach in the Career Services Center Professionalism: Ability to maintain confidentiality and comply with FERPA regulations Maintains reliability, accountability, and a strong work ethic Ability to follow university policies, office procedures, and written and verbal instructions Represents Career Services in a professional manner and maintains a welcoming office environment Uses good judgment when handling sensitive information and referring concerns to Career Services or Housing staff Teamwork: Ability to collaborate effectively with student employees and Career Services staff Supports team projects, including events, employer engagement, campus outreach, and office operations Builds positive working relationships with students, alumni, employers, and campus partners Provides strong customer service in front-desk, event, and limited Housing-support settings Technology: Proficiency in Microsoft 365 applications, including Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams, and OneDrive Ability to learn and utilize Handshake for appointments, employer approvals, job postings, and student engagement activities Ability to use standard office technology, including computers, phones, printers, and copiers Uses university systems and digital information responsibly while maintaining accuracy and confidentiality Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you received a Federal Work-Study award letter for the current academic year? Yes No Unsure * Our office is open 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Monday-Friday. What hours would you be available to work weekly during our office hours if hired? (Reminder, you cannot work during scheduled class time) (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6442": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Marketing &amp; Communications Project Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Marketing & Communications Project Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Marketing & Communications Project Manager Position Summary The Marketing & Communications Project Manager (PM) serves within the Marketing & Communications Office in the Division of Enrollment Management. This role manages creative project intake, develops timelines, coordinates creative services, advertising, and promotional materials, and helps evaluate project effectiveness. The PM keeps internal and external marketing and communications projects organized, on schedule, and aligned with TXWES brand standards. As a brand expert, the PM advises clients on best practices, ensures style and graphic guidelines are followed, and upholds established quality standards. The role also supports the development and implementation of the campus visual branding strategy, including timely updates to campus kiosks, signage, and banners. Candidates must have experience managing multiple print and creative projects. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Project Management: Trains clients/departments around campus to use the Project Workflow project management software to submit video, photography, web, digital, and print design requests. Works with departments to collect all project information including target audience, conversion, deadlines, finalized copy, etc., then traffic the project through to the creative and digital team. Coordinates production schedules while helping the various departments stay updated on project statuses. Serves as the MarComm representative on designated committees, providing strategic input and identifying committee needs that require MarComm support. Processes job completion through internal review, client review, final deliverable, and assessment of project with client after completion. (Daily, 60% of time) Print & Promotional Vendor Management: Develops and maintains relationships with print and promotional vendors. Works with vendors to organize the timely production of print campaigns and promotional items. (Daily, 25% of time) Campus Signage: Responsible for maintaining all branded public spaces. Manages regular checks on campus branding and works with vendors and facilities to repair and update signage. (Weekly, 15% of time) Support Marketing & Communications Projects: Support the marketing and communications team projects such as website updates, creative brainstorms, survey creations, copywriting, etc. Performs other related duties and projects as assigned. (As needed) Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Bachelor’s degree required. Knowledge of basic creative services including graphic design, social media and copyrighting is preferred. Experience Experience managing production schedules in a creative office or production environment. Knowledge of customer services best practices. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of print production process and experience sourcing promotional material. Strong organizational skills, and the ability to set, maintain, and meet deadlines. Ability to handle multiple tasks while maintaining high attention for details. Ability to prioritize and complete projects quickly/efficiently. Heavily oriented toward details/accuracy. Positive, motivated attitude. Ability to work independently and exercise good judgment. Ability to maintain a positive approach under pressure. Outstanding interpersonal and community relations skills. Ability to use discretion in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy and security regulations. Ability to adhere to university and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1122P Posting Open Date 07/06/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6293": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool-Graduate Programs of Nursing Practice",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool-Graduate Programs of Nursing Practice Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Adjunct Instructor Pool-Graduate Programs of Nursing Practice Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications for adjunct positions are reviewed as part-time faculty assignments become available. Adjunct positions are posted as pools and do not necessarily reflect our current adjunct needs. Pooled applications are reviewed based on adjunct need. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Instructor Pool-Graduate Programs of Nursing Practice Position Summary The Adjunct Family Nurse Practitioner Program faculty member is responsible for course development and teaching (including clinical supervision as appropriate) in online Graduate Programs in Nursing Practice. Responsibilities include assisting the Program Director in developing courses within an innovative curriculum, delivering instruction within scope of expertise, helping to ensure adherence to accreditation and regulatory expectations. Applicants must be open to including evidence-based, complementary, and integrative approaches as appropriate in courses taught, and support a culture of self-care for students. Applicants with diverse expertise are invited and considered based upon current needs of the program. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Develops, implements, maintains, and evaluates Graduate Nursing courses as assigned. Prepares learning experiences and delivers instruction for online graduate level nursing courses. Develops clinical practicum partnerships and supervises students in clinical practicum experiences (as appropriate within workload assignment). Adheres to the established class schedule and office hours requirements. Submits contracts, book requests, syllabi, grades, evaluations, and other required paperwork and reports in a timely manner Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Earned doctorate in nursing (doctoral candidates who will complete degree within 12 months of hire are eligible to apply); certification as a Family Nurse Practitioner (or related area as accepted by accrediting body); and unencumbered license (or eligible for approval) as an advanced practice nurse in Texas are required. Experience Experience as a faculty member in a nursing higher education program is required. Experience as a faculty member for a graduate nursing program is preferred. Experience in online education is preferred. Experience as a practicing advanced practice nurse is required. On-going certification during employment is required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of: -Thorough understanding of Family Nurse Practitioner practice models, national standards, professional issues and their application. -Thorough understanding of effective pedagogical approaches. -Basic understanding of online educational approaches. -Familiarity with academic policies and procedures of higher education institutions. -Thorough understanding of the rules, standards, regulations and laws related to student and patient information and records including FERPA and HIPPA . Skill in: Ability to develop new Graduate Nursing courses with innovative approaches that value relationship centered and whole-person care. Ability to develop and work with an inter-professional team to bring concepts of mind body-spirit connections, relationship-centered patient care, self-care, and practice management to the curriculum. -Ability to model desired professional practice. -Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. -Ability to demonstrate and provide excellent service to both the University and the community. -Ability to work effectively with other University personnel. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS917P Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Applications for adjunct positions are reviewed as part-time faculty assignments become available. Adjunct positions are posted as pools and do not necessarily reflect our current adjunct needs. Pooled applications are reviewed based on adjunct need. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). 1.\tWhat is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) 2.\tHow do you bring a sense of the whole person (mind-body-spirit) into your practice? (Open Ended Question) 3.\tWhat is your philosophy of self-care for the professional in supporting resilience? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) Letter of Recommendation Education Certification (if necessary) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6376": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool – School of Arts and Sciences",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool – School of Arts and Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Adjunct Instructor Pool – School of Arts and Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Instructor Pool – School of Arts and Sciences Position Summary Designs and delivers instruction in primarily undergraduate courses offered by the School of Arts and Sciences. Participates in all department, various schools, and University-wide tasks and activities. Disciplines include: Art Biochemistry Biology Chemistry Computer Information Systems. Computer Science Criminal Justice English Geology History Mass Communications Mathematics Music (History/Theory/Applied) Paralegal Studies Political Science Psychology Religion (Interfaith, Comparative and Christian Studies) Sociology Spanish Theater Essential Duties and Responsibilities Prepares lessons and delivers instruction primarily for undergraduate courses. Adheres to the faculty handbook and faculty guide. Meets classes for the required time and days in accordance with polices established for class schedule. Holds required office hours, keeps attendance, submits contracts, book requests, syllabi, grades, evaluations, and other required paperwork and reports in a timely manner. Remains knowledgeable of current research activities in respective discipline by reading journal articles, attending conferences, and maintaining relationships with other fellow researchers. Participates in curriculum assessment. Other duties as assigned by the Dean or Department Chair Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Masters degree, with a minimum of 18 hours in the discipline being taught. Experience Preferred, prior teaching experience at the college or university level preferred with evidence of teaching excellence. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to work effectively with other University personnel. Ability to provide service to both the University and the community. Ability to comply with rules, standards, regulations and laws related to student records. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to use discretion in handling confidential and sensitive matters. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret standard periodicals, professional journals, and/or governmental regulations. Ability to write reports, academic correspondence, and procedure manuals. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, students, and University employees. Ability to calculate figures & amounts such as discounts, interest, commissions, proportions, percentages, area, & volume. Ability to apply concepts of basic algebra, geometry, calculus and statistics. Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS758P Posting Open Date 04/02/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the discipline(s) that you are interested in applying for.  NOTE:  You must have transcripts verifying at least 18 hours of coursework in the discipline being taught. Communications Liberal Studies Humanities Theatre Music (History/Theory) Music (Applied) English French Spanish Religion (Christian Studies) Religion (Comparative Studies) Please select the discipline(s) that you are interested in applying for.  NOTE:  You must have transcripts verifying at least 18 hours of coursework in the discipline being taught. Biology Chemistry/Biochemistry Computer Science Criminal Justice History Mathematics Paralegal Studies Political Science Psychology Sociology Computer Information Systems * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No * Are you available to work weekends? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Do you live or plan on working outside the state of Texas? Yes No * If “Yes” to the question above, what city and state? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) Letter of Recommendation 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
