    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6336": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Maintenance Mechanic II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Maintenance Mechanic II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Maintenance Mechanic II Position Summary Under general supervision, the Maintenance Technician II is responsible for minor fabrication of water supply and drain pipe repair, installation of electrical controls, rerouting of electrical wiring, testing and diagnostics of circuitry components and the replacement of electrical equipment. Perform simple carpentry construction, including layout and design. Capable of lock, key, door and window repair. Performs preventative maintenance on HVAC units, automobile, and landscape equipment as assigned to him according to the prescribed standard of quality and identified procedures. Is subject to being recalled to campus for “after hours” work during the work week and weekend. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Various plumbing duties including welding, soldering, cutting, threading and gluing 2. Replacement of lights, fixtures, switches, receptacles, fuses, contactors, ballasts, starters, motors, pumps 3. Preforms preventive maintenance on HVAC equipment, and diagnostics of performance 4. Work with hand tools, power tools, torches, and electrical testing equipment 5. Performs preventive maintenance on machinery and equipment. 6. Completes work orders, equipment logs and other documentation 7. Other duties as assigned Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Must have a valid Texas Drivers license. Experience Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Outstanding interpersonal skills with excellent customer service orientation. • Ability to work effectively, diplomatically and professionally with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. • Ability to exercise judgment in establishing and executing priorities. • Ability to understand and meet customers’ needs and expectations. • Knowledge of and confidence in event operations. • Strong time management skills with the ability to meet deadlines. • Strong detail orientation. • Ability to adhere to University & departmental policies and procedures. • Ability to work independently with minimum supervision. • Ability to maintain a neat and clean workspace. • Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and events in a fluid, changing environment. • Ability to react calmly and effectively in emergency situations. • Ability to read and comprehend simple instructions, short correspondence, memos, blue prints and schematic. Ability to write simple correspondence. Ability to effectively present information in one-on-one and small group situations to customers, clients, and other employees of the organization. • Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. Ability to compute rate, ratio, and percent and to draw and interpret graphs. • Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1069P Posting Open Date 04/22/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6483": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Assistant Director of Alumni Relations",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Assistant Director of Alumni Relations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Assistant Director of Alumni Relations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Director of Alumni Relations Position Summary Plan and manage events specific to the office of alumni relations; manage communications including social media accounts; work with the director of alumni relations to plan and execute alumni programming. Areas of focus will include event planning and promotion, alumni engagement, digital communications and targeted alumni programming. The ideal candidate should be an enthusiastic and creative communications and/or event professional with experience in constituent engagement and relationship-building and a desire to connect with and provide amazing experiences for TXWES alumni. This role must be able to multi-task, stay organized and adjust to changes all while having fun and working collaboratively. Essential Duties and Responsibilities 1. Manage events specific to the Office of Advancement and Alumni Relations. Event planning should include, but is not limited to, the following tasks. · Serve as project manager, setting and maintaining timelines, priorities, and checklists for all events · Serve as point of contact to third-party vendors for catering, event rentals, photographers, etc., and internal constituencies including marketing, security, and IT · Research and book event venues · Oversee mailing lists, invitation process, and RSVPs · Manage internal and external event promotion, including electronic and printed pieces · Oversee all aspects of on-site event needs, including staffing, to ensure that event setup and teardown are done in a timely and organized fashion, devising alternative options for unseen circumstances such as inclement weather, etc. · Collaborate with campus partners, when applicable, to ensure event tasks are well-defined, designated to appropriate personnel, and documented · Gather quantitative and qualitative data for the event to support continuous quality improvement 2. Work with Marketing & Communications to: · Compile and submit complete information for promotional and print materials using their software program and comply with their deadlines. · Proactively ensure a consistent University brand is maintained through all promotional materials and on-site at events. Work with outside vendors on the ordering or promotional items. 3. Manage social media content across multiple platforms and develop strategies to enhance alumni engagement. 4. Create and implement strategic plans to engage alumni through various methods. Engage individual alumni through personal visits and communication. 5. Assist with Alumni Board management and oversee the alumni scholarship process. Engage individual alumni through personal visits and communication. 6. Manage alumni communications calendar and draft text for event promotions to be used on the University calendar, print and e-mail promotions, and various online platforms. 7. Establish event follow-up process, including, but not limited to the following: · Analyzing event performance through post-event meetings with internal and external stakeholders, surveys, and other means necessary · Utilizing feedback to continually improve event performance · Sending thank you correspondence to attendees, hosts, volunteers, etc. · Collaboration with donor relations on post-event stewardship opportunities 8. Supervise office student worker(s), when applicable. 9. Other duties as assigned by the vice president of advancement or the director of alumni relations. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Required: · Bachelor’s degree. · Three (3) years of experience in planning and coordinating events and/or communications. · Proficient knowledge of utilizing social media platforms – primarily Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn – for program and event promotions, and constituent engagement. · Experience in planning and assessment, including formulation, development, implementation, and evaluation. Experience Preferred: · Previous employment at a university or college, preferably in university advancement or alumni relations. · Experience with Raiser’s Edge data software and/or Blackbaud NetCommunity. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities · Ability to work evenings and weekends. · Ability to plan, prioritize tasks, and meet deadlines. · Ability to handle highly confidential, sensitive issues with diplomacy and discretion, while complying with FERPA & privacy regulations. · Knowledge of basic public relations and communications principles. · Knowledge of standard office practices and procedures. · Excellent written and verbal communication skills. · Proficient in the use of Microsoft Office and Adobe products. · Proficiency with an integrated administrative system and current software programs. · Proficient use of multi-line phone system and standard office equipment. · Ability to adhere to University and departmental procedures and policies. · Ability to work independently in the most efficient manner with minimum supervision. · Proven interpersonal skills to provide support in a high-profile office with tact and diplomacy. · Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. · Ability to provide and demonstrate quality customer service. · Strong organizational skills with the ability to handle multiple tasks. · Great attention to detail with an eye towards accuracy. · Ability to exercise judgment in establishing and executing priorities. · Ability to demonstrate problem-solving techniques quickly when necessary. · Skill in budget preparation, fiscal management, and utilizing resources. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1126P Posting Open Date 08/17/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No Are you available to work weekends? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
