    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6490": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | New Student Mentor (2026-2027) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us New Student Mentor (2026-2027) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If you would like assistance with your resume, cover letter, or other application materials, please contact Career Services at careerservices@txwes.edu. Application will remain open until filled, however, Priority Deadline for Consideration: Sept. 18. 2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title New Student Mentor (2026-2027) Position Summary The New Student Mentor works as a member of the TXWES Orientation team and serves as a peer leader who supports the planning and facilitation of New Student Registration Days and Ram Camp. This position helps incoming students transition successfully to Texas Wesleyan University by building relationships, leading small groups through the orientation experience, and modeling positive, professional, and welcoming customer service. The position also helps the student employee build leadership, communication, and event-support skills while supporting the university’s mission of student success. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Build relationships with new students to support their transition to Texas Wesleyan University, serving as an approachable, positive, and reliable point of contact throughout the orientation process. Lead a small group of new students throughout their orientation experience, guiding them through Ram Camp and New Student Registration Days activities and helping them build connections with peers. Attend and actively participate in all required trainings during the semester and summer, and all Orientation dates, including Ram Camp and mid-year and summer New Student Registration Days. Work with fellow New Student Mentors and Orientation staff to plan, coordinate, and carry out welcome weekend activities that help incoming students feel supported and included. Encourage and support students, student organizations, academic departments, and campus programs by promoting events and initiatives that benefit the student community and align with the university’s mission. Cultivate and maintain positive, professional working relationships with staff, faculty, and students, and participate in ongoing student leadership development trainings and workshops. Adhere to all university and departmental policies and guidelines, complete other assigned duties, and protect confidential student information in accordance with FERPA . Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Must be enrolled as a student in good standing at Texas Wesleyan University, maintain a minimum semester GPA of 2.0 & cumulative GPA of 2.5 throughout the completion of the contract, and maintain eligibility for student employment in accordance with university policies. Ability to attend all mandatory trainings, New Student Registration Days, and Ram Camp sessions throughout the summer and academic year. Experience Demonstrated experience in orientation, student leadership, event planning, or involvement in student organizations. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrates initiative by seeking opportunities to grow through leadership and mentorship experiences Ability to balance collaborative and independent work effectively Shows adaptability while supporting a wide range of new-student needs Takes ownership of assigned responsibilities and follows through in a timely manner Excellent written, oral, social media-based, and interpersonal communication skills Ability to discern student needs and respond in a caring, supportive manner Ability to articulate enthusiasm and support for all students within the campus community Outstanding interpersonal and community-building skills Ability to assess student needs during orientation and respond using sound judgment Knowledge and ability to complete assigned tasks thoroughly, appropriately, and in a timely manner Ability to be creative and bring new ideas to the position Possession of strong organizational skills Ability to lead effectively and instruct others in a group setting Demonstrated experience in, or aptitude for, student leadership and event planning encouraged Ability to encourage others and actively participate in the campus community Models a positive, high-energy, and welcoming approach to New Student Programs and Orientation. Ability to be discreet in handling confidential matters while complying with FERPA regulations Ability to adhere to all university and departmental policies and procedures Maintains reliability, accountability, and a strong work ethic Ability to attend all mandatory meetings and trainings Ability to work independently and in a team setting in an efficient manner Ability to demonstrate a cooperative attitude while collaborating with a diverse student population Cultivates and maintains good working relationships with staff, faculty, and fellow mentors Ability to articulate passion and support for all students, honoring the diverse backgrounds and experiences represented within the student community Basic knowledge of Outlook, Word, and Excel Ability to communicate effectively using social media and digital platforms Ability to learn and utilize university systems and technology to support Orientation programming Uses technology responsibly to support communication and event coordination Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 08/20/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date 09/23/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants If you would like assistance with your resume, cover letter, or other application materials, please contact Career Services at careerservices@txwes.edu. Application will remain open until filled, however, Priority Deadline for Consideration: Sept. 18. 2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your overall GPA? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a 2.5 cumulative grade point average or higher? Yes No * Do you qualify for work-study funds? Yes No Not sure Please explain your previous involvement with TXWES Orientation and years served. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) List of Three References Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
