    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/5942": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Content Producer for Rambler Media Group (Student Assistant and Work Study)",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Content Producer for Rambler Media Group (Student Assistant and Work Study) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Content Producer for Rambler Media Group (Student Assistant and Work Study) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a writing sample, either a cover letter for your application or other work that you have written personally. This work must NOT be AI generated. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Content Producer for Rambler Media Group (Student Assistant and Work Study) Position Summary Come work with student media. The Content Producer will produce at least two stories per week for all Rambler-related entities, including packages for online and YouTube presentation. Content Producers should provide consistent and accurate coverage of Texas Wesleyan and Texas Wesleyan-related events. Content Producers must become familiar with The Rambler policies manual and statement of ethical behavior in student media. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Specific duties include: - Produce at least two publishable assignments each week in text, video, slideshow, podcast, interactive graphic, interactive map or other media mode based on appropriateness for each story. - Meet deadlines. - Generate and communicate to Editor-in-Chief, Faculty Adviser and Faculty Liaison newsworthy story ideas on a weekly basis during budget meetings. - Maintain contact and good rapport with sources from beats. - Conduct interviews and research to ensure balanced, complete, fair and accurate stories. - Provide a complete list of all sources, including contact information, for quality control purposes. - Make revisions to edited stories in a timely fashion for same-day turnaround. - Attend regularly scheduled meetings for all staff, including training sessions. - Seek individual help or training when problems arise. - Maintain Rambler equipment to ensure proper functioning, availability and cleanliness. - Keep up with email, phone messages and campus mail with next-day turnaround. - Post to Rambler social media as needed. - Practice basics of convergent journalism through The Rambler, www.therambler.org and Rambler TV so that appropriate story is filed with appropriate media outlet. - Adhere to all Rambler social media policies. Other duties as assigned, including rotating Editor-in-Chief possibility for print edition. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses None required. Experience No prior experience is necessary, but a desire to learn is required. Content Producers must familiarize themselves with The Rambler policies manual and statement of ethical behavior in student media. Students will be required to write, shoot photographs, create videos, produce podcasts and create social media posts. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of Associated Press Style and use of digital media is a plus. Knowledge of WordPress, Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign is also a plus. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a writing sample, either a cover letter for your application or other work that you have written personally. This work must NOT be AI generated. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you qualify for Federal work study? yes no How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No Are you available to work weekends? Yes No Please select your current grade level. Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student Have you ever worked on Campus before? Yes No Do you plan on working anywhere else on campus? If so, please list where. (Open Ended Question) Do you have experiences with using Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator or any other photography/videography softwares? Please explain. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Portfolio 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6498": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Global Admissions Specialist",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Global Admissions Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Global Admissions Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Global Admissions Specialist Position Summary The Global Admissions Specialist works as a member of the Graduate and Global Team in support of admission of both international undergraduate, international graduate and domestic graduate students. Responsibilities include managing, processing, and evaluating admission documents, maintaining consistent communication with prospective and active students, while providing administrative support to the populations that the department serves. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Process, manage, file, and update applicant records in the CRM system accurately and efficiently. Serve as a Designated School Official ( DSO ), issuing I-20’s and ensuring compliance with SEVP regulations. Communicate with and support students throughout the enrollment funnel through international admissions inbox, telephone, and in person. Serve as counselor for undergraduate international students, assisting with registration outreach Monitor and resolve data integrity issues on an ongoing basis; perform audits across the admissions funnel Collaborate with team for student orientation and associated events Collaborate with team for recruitment opportunities and outreach targeting international and graduate student populations. Other duties as assigned by Director of Graduate and Global Recruitment Education, Certifications and/or Licenses A bachelor’s degree from an accredited college Experience Experience in international admissions, international compliance, enrollment management, or related field preferred Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated ability to work and communicate with team members Demonstrated ability to maintain positive relationships Must have expert written, verbal, analytical and organizational skills Knowledge and comfort with use of Slate CRM or related technology preferred Knowledge of SEVP regulations and experience as a DSO preferred Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1127P Posting Open Date 08/25/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have experience working with international students, either on the admission or student support side? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6389": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Dean of Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Dean of Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Dean of Education Position Summary The Dean of Education is charged with establishing, implementing, and evaluating the strategic priorities of the School of Education. The Dean reports directly to the Provost and Senior Vice President of Academic Affairs and provides leadership to the program directors, faculty, and staff in the School of Education. Working with the program directors, the Dean is responsible for the School’s academic program quality, assessment of curriculum and instruction, fostering faculty research and scholarship, budgeting and fiscal management, fundraising, and new program development. Successful candidates must possess a record of academic and scholarly excellence that meets or exceeds the University’s criteria for appointment as a full professor. The start date for this position is August 1, 2026 Essential Duties and Responsibilities Leadership & Strategic Direction Provide leadership and direction to instructional and program staff, faculty, and adjunct faculty in developing and sustaining programs, instructional strategies, and program offerings. Administer and maintain accurate records for students, faculty and support staff, such as advising reports, professional development plans, annual evaluations and other personnel records as appropriate for specific program needs and responsibilities of the school. Develop goals and objectives for programs and participate in implementing accountability systems to ensure alignment with policies and procedures. Provide input to the Provost on long-range and strategic planning activities. Recommend employment, retention, promotion, and termination of instructors and staff to the Provost. Assist in resolving faculty and staff issues, including student grievances, academic integrity, and safety concerns. Serve as chair for the steering committee of the Leadership Academy Network (1882 partnership) and provide guidance and oversight for the LAN Senior Director and staff. Curriculum & Program Oversight Lead the process of new program development and revision of existing programs, together with the faculty of the school in keeping with strategic planning initiatives and seek accreditation and approvals by relevant state, regional, national and professional accrediting agencies. Ensure assessment of student learning outcomes in accordance with University policies. Promote revenue growth through new initiatives, grants, and continuing education opportunities. Accreditation & Compliance Ensure timely completion of accreditation and program approval requirements. Coordinate and document required program approval and/or accreditation activities. Maintain active program advisory committees to guide School of Education programs. Operations & Resource Management Direct and oversee School operations, including budget planning, management, and faculty loads/contracts. Supervise the school budget, approve requisitions and travel requests, and submit annual budget requests to the Provost. In conjunction with program directors, plan and coordinate course schedules to meet student needs and enrollment targets, optimizing faculty loads, budgets, and space. Lead development of a data-informed, student-centered master schedule to support student completion and workforce alignment. Support Advancement fundraising activities and initiatives in addition to developing a compelling vision for the school, cultivating relationships with donors, and strategically aligning fundraising efforts with institutional goals. Communication & Representation Represent the School of Education to partners (ISDs, TEA , etc.), external agencies, and professional/community groups. Coordinate with Marketing and Communications to develop and implement a marketing strategy for the School’s programs. Communicate policies, standards, and expectations to faculty and staff, and hold employees accountable. Build and maintain positive working relationships with University colleagues and external partners. Actively serve on internal and external task forces, committees, and work groups. Attend internal and external events to represent the School of Education. These include but are not limited to graduation, honors ceremonies, open houses, orientation, meetings with leadership teams in school districts. Administrative Duties Collaborate in developing policies, practices, processes, and programs for the School. Participate in professional development appropriate to the position. Schedule and preside over School meetings and maintain meeting minutes. Monitor instruction, conduct performance appraisals, and assist with professional development planning. Research and prepare technical and administrative reports and written correspondence. Work in conjunction with the Vice President for Finance, Vice President for Enrollment and other university departments in developing and monitoring initiatives for student enrollment and retention, including budget preparation. Other duties as assigned. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Dean must have earned academic doctorate, and appropriate professional and clinical credentials in a discipline represented in or related to the School of Education. Experience Requires a minimum of five years of full-time experience within Texas public schools and higher education institutions. Higher education experience is expected. A record of successful administrative leadership at the dean, chair, or program director level, including budget and personnel experience or other related administrative experience Experience with professionally accredited academic programs and familiarity with compliance and risk management practices. Experience with clinical site development and oversight including creating partnerships integral to student field experiences A data informed planner with experience in assessment and outcomes measurements. A record of advanced learning, innovation, or teaching experience incorporating both traditional and distance education programs Experience working with external agencies, such as foundations, local businesses, and governmental agencies Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge, skills, and abilities commensurate with key responsibilities. Knowledge of the Texas Education Agency requirements for teacher education programs and experience with curricular design or redesign to meet these requirements. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1099P Posting Open Date 04/20/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * Will you have a Ph.D. in hand by the date of appointment or an advanced ABD by the date of the appointment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) List of Three References 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6368": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool - School of Business",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool - School of Business Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Adjunct Instructor Pool - School of Business Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Instructor Pool - School of Business Position Summary Disciplines include: Accounting, General Business, Finance, Forensic Accounting/Fraud, Data Analytics, Management, Marketing, Business Law, Health Care Management, and Supply Chain Management. Designs and delivers instruction in primarily undergraduate courses offered by the School of Business. Participates in all department, various schools, and University-wide tasks and activities. Applications for adjunct positions are reviewed as part-time faculty assignments become available. Adjunct positions are posted as pools and do not necessarily reflect our current adjunct needs. Pooled applications are reviewed based on adjunct need. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Prepares lessons and delivers instruction primarily for undergraduate courses. Adheres to the faculty handbook and faculty guide. Meets classes for the required time and days in accordance with polices established for class schedule. Holds required office hours and submits contracts, book requests, syllabi, grades, evaluations, and other required paperwork and reports in a timely manner. Remains knowledgeable of current research activities in respective discipline by reading journal articles, attending conferences, and maintaining relationships with other fellow researchers. Participates in curriculum assessment. Other duties as assigned by the Dean or Associate Dean. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Master’s degree, with preferably 18 hours in the discipline being taught and related work experience or a licensed CPA with appropriate work experience for Accounting courses. Experience Prior teaching experience at the college or university level preferred with evidence of teaching excellence, or related work experience Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to work effectively with other University personnel. Ability to provide service to both the University and the community. Ability to comply with rules, standards, regulations and laws related to student records. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to use discretion in handling confidential and sensitive matters. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, and/or governmental regulations. Ability to write reports, business correspondence, and procedure manuals. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, students, and University employees. Ability to calculate figures & amounts such as discounts, interest, commissions, proportions, percentages, area, & volume. Ability to apply concepts of basic algebra, geometry, calculus and statistics. Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS782P Posting Open Date 01/01/2026 Open Until Filled Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been an online instructor for a credit course? (Open Ended Question) * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * Please select the discipline(s) that you are interested in applying for. NOTE: You must have transcripts verifying at least 18 hours of coursework in the discipline being taught, or previous work experience.\r\no\tAccounting\r\no\tData Analytics \r\no\tGeneral Business\r\no\tFinance\r\no\tForensic Accounting/Fraud\r\no\tManagement\r\no\tMarketing\r\no\tBusiness Law\r\no\tHealthcare Management\r\no\tSupply Chain Management (Open Ended Question) * If any, briefly list all prior university- or college-level coursework that you have taught. (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No * Do you live or plan on working outside the state of Texas? Yes No * If “Yes” to the question above, what city and state? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Education Certification (if necessary) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/5708": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Academic Success Center Financial Accounting Tutor (Student Assistant or Work Study position)",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Academic Success Center Financial Accounting Tutor (Student Assistant or Work Study position) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Academic Success Center Financial Accounting Tutor (Student Assistant or Work Study position) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Academic Success Center Financial Accounting Tutor (Student Assistant or Work Study position) Position Summary Provides academic tutoring services for financial accounting to students on an individual basis or in small groups. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide academic tutoring services by maintaining a weekly schedule of available hours for appointments. Attend tutor training workshops as required. Keep accurate records of tutoring appointments by filing tutoring reports. Maintain contact with professors in your subject of expertise in order to obtain pertinent materials for the ASC . Assist undergraduate students with assignments. Tutoring appointments are intended to assists students in becoming better students. Assist with additional duties as needed such as, covering the front desk, scheduling tutoring appointments, answering phones, organizing materials and maintaining information in the ASC . Education, Certifications and/or Licenses High school diploma/ GED required. Successfully completed courses in subject area tutoring with a grade of “A” or “B” at Texas Wesleyan (exceptions upon discretion of the Director). Minimum GPA of 3.0 (exceptions upon discretion of the Director). Experience Formal or informal tutoring experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters pertaining to student’s privacy. Ability to work independently in an efficient manner. Ability to instruct others. Strong interpersonal skills. Demonstrate knowledge and competence in the subject matter. Enjoy tutoring the subject for which services are being provided. Effectively communicate study strategies to ensure academic success. Work comfortably with people from various backgrounds. Exhibit patience and positive attitudes in the learning environment. Ability to provide and demonstrate quality customer service. Pleasant and clearly understandable phone voice. Strong organizational skills to work productively. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy ( FERPA ) regulations. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 08/28/2024 Open Until Filled Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
