    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6121": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Summer Operations Assistant",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Summer Operations Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Summer Operations Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Summer Operations Assistant Position Summary Operations Assistants are responsible for overseeing summer housing groups that are utilizing residence halls and facilities. They are responsible for managing camp and conference operations including scheduling and managing groups that are arriving to campus and assisting with New Student Orientation Registration Days. They are also responsible for completing projects assigned by Residence Life Professional Staff. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Attend summer meetings each week. Manage check-ins and triage issues. Manage communication with all housing groups. Manage placement for all housing groups. Prepare materials and scheduling for all group check-ins including flyers, keys, etc. Communicate camp dates, needs, and other necessary information to the staff. Work with Residence Life Staff on any billing regarding camp and conference participants. Communicate well with staff, parents, students, and camp leaders, and departments organizing housing groups. Work on Facilities projects Assist with the room key audit, preparation, and inventory Assist in residence hall key audit Attend and assist with New Student Orientation Registration Days Assist in managing Facilities Assistant projects Due to the constant changes to the working environment in this position, additional duties may be added or retracted from the current job description at the time the need arises. The student will be informed upon changes. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Experience Must have and maintain both a cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5 Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Outstanding interpersonal and community building skills. Strong customer service skills. Effective team member participation and leadership. Ability to resolve conflicts while being fair and consistent with students especially in discipline matters. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy ( FERPA ) regulations. Ability to demonstrate a cooperative attitude. Possession of organizational skills. Ability to discern student needs and respond in a caring manner. Ability to maintain composure in challenging situations or emergencies. Ability to encourage others and participate in the community. Knowledge and ability to complete given tasks and assignments thoroughly, appropriately, and in a timely manner. Ability to ask questions to help solve issues, problems, and or conflicts. Ability to Interpret and disseminate information and directives. Ability to read and comprehend instructions, short correspondence, and memos. Ability to write standard correspondence. Ability to effectively present information in one-on-one and small group situations to current and prospective students and University employees. Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. Ability to work with a rotating schedule consisting of weekends, late nights, and holidays. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 02/02/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What experiences do you have that prepared you for this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6404": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Cross-Country Track &amp; Field Head Coach Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Cross-Country Track & Field Head Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Cross-Country Track & Field Head Coach Position Summary The head coach is responsible for all aspects of the intercollegiate track and cross-country program. Essential Duties and Responsibilities •\tRecruit and maintain a quota of qualified student-athletes who meet the requirements for entrance into Texas Wesleyan University. •\tHire, train, and supervise assistant or student assistant coaches. •\tResponsible for fundraising for appropriate dollar amounts through donations or special projects. •\tCoach his/her team. •\tOversee the student-athletes GPA requirements each semester. •\tDevelop a yearly budget and control spending to ensure the sport is not over budget. •\tSchedule all contests including scrimmages. •\tBe familiar with the eligibility requirements for NAIA student athletes and teams and submit required documentation in a timely manner. •\tComplete accurate monthly reports in a timely manner. •\tSupervise student-athletes during practice and games to ensure that the highest standards of sportsmanship and integrity are maintained. •\tDevelop, write and administer a yearly plan. •\tEvaluate his/her intercollegiate athletic program continuously. •\tArrange for all athletic awards in his/her area. •\tRepresent the University in public presentations as needed. •\tConduct outreach activity(s) in the local community. •\tArrange safe transportation for all away contests. •\tAttend clinics and workshops to achieve certification and/or keep skills current. •\tAssist in the coordination of the departments special activities. •\tServe on committees as assigned by Provost or Athletic Director. •\tAvailable for varied hours, including: weekends and evenings/holidays. •\tWhile performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly exposed to outside weather conditions. •\tOther duties assigned by the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses •\tBachelor’s degree required, Masters preferred. •\tMinimum three years experience in coaching sport at collegiate or university level or equivalency at lower level. •\tA valid Texas Driver’s License required. Experience Minimum three years of experience in coaching sport at collegiate or university level or equivalency at lower level preferred. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities •\tKnowledge of sport coaching required, where available certification preferred. •\tFamiliarity with NAIA policies and procedures is preferred. •\tAbility and authority to drive a 15-passenger van, i.e. a safe driving record. •\tAbility to write neatly and accurately. •\tAbility to demonstrate appropriate technical skills during practice. •\tAbility to apply common sense understanding to carry out detailed but uninvolved written or oral instructions. •\tAbility to deal with problems involving a few concrete variables in standardized situations. •\tAbility to read and comprehend instructions, short correspondence, and memos. •\tAbility to write correspondence. •\tAbility to effectively present information in one-on-one and small group situations to customers, clients, and other University employees. •\tInstructing student-athletes relative to specific skill necessary to compete in collegiate sport. •\tAbility to read, analyze, and interpret financial reports, legal documents, general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures, or governmental regulations •\tAbility to respond to common inquiries or complaints from customers, regulatory agencies, or members of the business community. •\tAbility to effectively present information to Senior Staff, public groups, managers and employees. •\tAbility to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. •\tAbility to be discrete in handling confidential matters, while complying with FERPA regulations. •\tAbility to complete all physical tasks as needed. •\tAbility to be able to work evenings, weekends, and possible holidays. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1108P Posting Open Date 05/18/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD Do you possess a valid Texas driver's license? Yes No Are you available to work rotating shifts including days, nights, weekends and holiday? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) Letter of Recommendation Education Certification (if necessary) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
