    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6469": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Student Employee for Advancement Office Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Student Employee for Advancement Office Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Documents Needed to Apply: Financial Aid Award Letter, Class Schedule Posting Details Position Information Job Title Student Employee for Advancement Office Position Summary The Office of Advancement is seeking a motivated and creative student to support the programs and objectives of the Advancement Office, specifically Annual Giving, including four mini campaigns, the Annual Day of Giving Campaign and event, and the day-to-day operational support of donor relations and engagement. This position offers a unique opportunity for a student interested in marketing, communications, non-profit management, or digital media to gain hands-on experience contributing to live campaigns. While the student will primarily work with the Annual Giving Director, they will have the opportunity to collaborate with an entire team of fundraising professionals and gain hands-on experience for their resume or CV. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assist in the development and execution of four email, digital and mass mailing mini campaigns throughout the year. Support internal data collection and posting to Raiser’s Edge, the Advancement CRM . Calendar and process monthly requirements, such as donor birthday cards, New Employee Orientation packets, etc. Manage Advancement social media platforms under the supervision of the Annual Giving Director or Annual Giving intern. Serve as a vital member of the Advancement team, assisting with event set-up, administrative details and creative brainstorming Assist with basic analytics tracking and reporting Serve as a front desk receptionist for the department Other duties as assigned by the Annual Giving Director Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Experience Junior preferred to work for two years with a major in Business, Marketing, Communications, Media, or related field, or interest in non-profit management. If you are not a junior, but inerested, please feel free to apply. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Graphic design Social media content development Microsoft Office Experience with and/or interest in: Graphic design Social media content development Microsoft Office CRM’s and/or willingness to learn Giving platforms and/or willingness to learn Comfort using AI tools as a support resource Strong attention to detail and ability to follow established branding guidelines Ability to work independently and manage time effectively within a flexible schedule Ability to handle confidential matters in a professional manner Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Documents Needed to Apply: Financial Aid Award Letter, Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you eligible for Work Study? Yes No Please select your current grade level. Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student What is your major? (Open Ended Question) Have you ever worked on Campus before? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6210": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | PEER MENTOR (Undergraduate Student Position)",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | PEER MENTOR (Undergraduate Student Position) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us PEER MENTOR (Undergraduate Student Position) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. After the online application, selected applicants will be invited to an interview and be given an opportunity to deliver a presentation on mentoring. Posting Details Position Information Job Title PEER MENTOR (Undergraduate Student Position) Position Summary Reporting to the faculty supervisor of the Peer Mentoring Studio, this position facilitates student success and learning through positive peer support. This position also builds leadership and mentoring skills for the student employee. The peer mentor is an undergraduate student who helps peers navigate the college environment and achieve their academic and personal goals through study skills, commitment, persistence, accountability, innovation, and integrity. The Peer Mentor role requires interaction with students inside and outside of the classroom as well as in the studio for consultations. Mentoring involves active and ongoing relationships between mentors and students being mentored to promote social and academic development. Essential Duties and Responsibilities • Meet with assigned students outside of class and in the Peer Mentoring Studio • Meet with faculty supervisor as needed to plan, implement, and assess engagement strategies. • Design and host study groups in the PM Studio. • Disseminate helpful information to peers; Effectively communicate strategies that foster academic success in oral and written communication. • Serve as a student role model who takes pride in Texas Wesleyan University and the Ramily; maintain knowledge of campus resources and campus events in order to encourage student attendance at events around campus. • Attend training sessions with faculty supervisor and professional development activities related to mentoring and student success. • Facilitate socio-academic experiences and walk-in support sessions. • Assist students in interacting with faculty members and with other audiences to foster college life-skill building. • Complete and submit workshop plans, voiceover presentations, and documents to be used with students in the PM (Peer Mentoring) Studio • Confer with faculty supervisor regarding necessary peer mentoring interventions and outreach. • Attend and participate in all training and staff meetings as required. • Attend the workplace regularly, reports to work punctually and follows a work schedule to keep up with the demands of the worksite, adhering to the advanced notice policy for absences from work. • Develop outreach materials and correspondence with faculty and staff to increase student retention efforts • Deliver presentations promoting peer mentoring in classes to raise awareness of available support. • Practice growing skills in writing goal-oriented action plans for student benefit and progress checks. • Create web content, social media posts, data entry, and documentation in spreadsheets for records of student contact. Proficiency in using the Microsoft Suite, presentation tools, and virtual meeting interfaces such as Teams and Zoom. • Collect attendance data for every peer mentoring consultation, including student names, course title, date, and time of session. •Have a class schedule that permits staffing hours for campus and student needs; ability to work during student-access-to- campus days; takes initiative in an active and visible role as a student leader on campus. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses • Current enrollment as a student in good standing at the university with a cumulative GPA near 3.0 or above. Experience • Completion of at least 15 credit hours at Texas Wesleyan University; faculty recommendation for social and communication skills and capacity to mentor peers with compassion and ethics; additional subject matter expertise in a student major preferred but not required. Experience • Previous experience in tutoring, mentoring, coaching, or assisting peers is preferred. • Experience developing problem-solving improvement plans preferred. • Skill in guiding student peers within the Canvas Course Management System • Experience documenting details through note-taking and/or record-keeping. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities • Ability to work independently when necessary and collaboratively with colleagues and faculty supervisor to develop a welcoming studio environment. • Confidentiality and discretion regarding student challenges. • Passion for helping others and motivation to help others succeed. • Ability to work with students from different backgrounds and with differentiated learning needs. • Strong time management and organizational skills. • Effective interpersonal and communication skills. • Ability to adhere to University and Studio policies and procedures. • Discretion in in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy ( FERPA ) regulations. • Ability to take perspective and to practice empathy. • Ability to practice active listening, craft engaging questions for students, and engage in mentoring and problem-solving in order to customize individual action plans and progress checks. • Ability to maintain a neat & professional appearance and office atmosphere. • Ability to read, write, and comprehend instructions, standard correspondence, and memos. • Ability to complete job tasks and assignments thoroughly, appropriately, and in a timely manner. • Ability to uphold workplace ethics and principles of academic integrity for student benefit. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 01/14/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants After the online application, selected applicants will be invited to an interview and be given an opportunity to deliver a presentation on mentoring. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) List of Three References Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6437": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Reference and Instruction Librarian Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Reference and Instruction Librarian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Reference and Instruction Librarian Position Summary This staff position serves as Department Head, providing leadership, strategic direction, and oversight for departmental services, personnel, and daily operations. Supervises and mentors department faculty and staff; coordinates workflows; supports professional development; and ensures departmental goals align with the mission and strategic priorities of the library and institution. Responsible for information and research services in all formats and venues, including reference, instruction, information commons, workshops, and related initiatives. Provides in-person and virtual information, research, and reference services. Plans, teaches, and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with faculty. Develops materials to support research and instruction for all teaching modalities. Pay Rate | Annual Salary | $59,000.00 Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provides leadership, supervision, and evaluation of department staff. Oversees departmental planning, goal setting, assessment, and reporting. Coordinates scheduling and coverage for reference, instruction, and service points. Facilitates departmental meetings and supports collaborative decision-making. Ensure alignment of departmental initiatives with library and institutional strategic goals. Recommends policies, procedures, and service improvements. Mentors and supports library faculty and staff for professional development. Plans, teaches, and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with faculty. Develops digital and print-based materials to support research and instruction in all formats. Creates tailored instruction at the request of faculty. Provides effective group and one-on-one instruction sessions in all modalities. Locates and creates digital content to support academic instruction. Prepares, provides, and creates assessment tools for engaging library instruction. Maintains current knowledge of citation styles, information retrieval tools, and teaching practices. Develops traditional and computer-assisted instructional tools to help users develop library, electronic, and internet research skills. Manages collection development for assigned academic programs and recommends library materials and databases as appropriate. Informs and instructs librarians regarding current reference materials, sources, and service delivery practices. Participates in the development and maintenance of the reference guides, instruction videos, and online research tools. Develops and updates both print and electronic instructional support materials. Explores, evaluates, and encourages the deployment of emerging technologies into library programs and services. Serves as a liaison to academic departments to strengthen course-integrated library instruction. Develops campus partnerships and interacts collegially with the campus community. Provides weekly evening reference assistance for students at the reference desk. Participates in continuing education, professional associations, and library committees. Serves on faculty committees as assigned. Performs related duties as assigned. NOTE : The above job description is intended to represent only the key areas of responsibility; specific position assignments will vary depending on the department’s business needs. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Master of Library Science from an ALA -accredited institution is required. Experience Experience working with various library resources is required. Experience working in a reference/instruction department in a library is required (5+ years). Experience in reference services for online programs is required. Experience in assessment strategies is preferred. Experience with Springshare software is preferred. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities (position requirements at entry) Knowledge of: Knowledge of instruction and research Knowledge of best practices for online pedagogy. Knowledge of learning techniques as they apply to library instruction. Skills : Ability to adhere to university and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to uphold our university’s core values. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Ability to work independently and efficiently to meet deadlines with minimum supervision. Ability to participate in a collaborative service-oriented environment. Ability to maintain a professional appearance and office atmosphere. Ability to provide and demonstrate excellent customer service. Ability to plan, prioritize tasks, and meet deadlines while working on multiple tasks. Proven interpersonal skills to provide support in a high-profile office with tact and diplomacy. Ability to maintain professionalism while working with diverse groups and in various situations. Ability to be discreet in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy regulations. Knowledge of rules, standards, regulations, and laws regarding student records. Ability to develop skills and remain knowledgeable of current trends in library services. Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. Ability to compute rate, ratio, and percent and to draw and interpret bar graphs. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS1117P Posting Open Date 06/15/2026 Open Until Filled Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a masters degree? Yes No How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Have you worked in an academic library before? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) Letter of Recommendation List of Three References 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6373": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool - Kinesiology",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool - Kinesiology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Adjunct Instructor Pool - Kinesiology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Instructor Pool - Kinesiology Position Summary Designs and delivers instruction in undergraduate courses offered by the Department of Kinesiology (as instructor education and experience allows), including but not limited to: courses in exercise science, physical education teacher preparation, recreation administration, first aid and safety, and activity/fitness. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Prepares lessons and delivers instruction. Adheres to the faculty handbook and faculty guide. Meets classes for the required time and days in accordance with policies established for class schedule. Submits attendance, grades and other required paperwork and reports in a timely manner. Please list area of expertise (i.e.. activity, exercise physiology, biomechanics, pedagogy, sport management) under school major. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Master’s Degree required: Earned Master’s Degree in Kinesiology, Exercise Science or related field or 18 Hours of course work in Kinesiology from an accredited institution. Activity courses may require specialized instructor certification. (ie. yoga, martial arts, scuba, WSI ) Experience Prior teaching experience and experience in the subject matter is preferred. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to work effectively with other University personnel. Ability to comply with rules, standards, regulations and laws related to student records. Ability to adhere to University and department policies and procedures. Ability to use discretion in handling confidential and sensitive issues, FERPA . Ability to work effectively with other University personnel. Ability to provide service to both the University and the community. Ability to comply with rules, standards, regulations and laws related to student records. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, and/or governmental regulations. Ability to write reports, business correspondence, and procedure manuals. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, students, and University employees. Ability to calculate figures & amounts such as discounts, interest, commissions, proportions, percentages, area, & volume. Ability to apply concepts of basic algebra, geometry, calculus and statistics. Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2016AS765P Posting Open Date 01/01/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Are you available to work weekends? Yes No * Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No * Please select the discipline(s) that you are interested in applying for.  NOTE:  You must have transcripts verifying at least 18 hours of coursework in the discipline being taught. Undergraduate Education Undergraduate Kinesiology Doctorate of Education Masters of Education * Do you live or plan on working outside the state of Texas? Yes No * If “Yes” to the question above, what city and state? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Current Employee Application (for internal applicants) Letter of Recommendation Education Certification (if necessary) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
