    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/5726": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | ASC Writing Tutor (Work Study or Student Assistant)",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | ASC Writing Tutor (Work Study or Student Assistant) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us ASC Writing Tutor (Work Study or Student Assistant) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title ASC Writing Tutor (Work Study or Student Assistant) Position Summary Provides academic tutoring services for writing to students on an individual basis or in small groups. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide academic tutoring services by maintaining a weekly schedule of available hours for appointments. Attend tutor training workshops as required. Keep accurate records of tutoring appointments by filing tutoring reports. Maintain contact with professors in your subject of expertise in order to obtain pertinent materials for the ASC . Assist undergraduate students with writing assignments such as, topic selection, formatting, citations, grammar and punctuation. Tutoring appointments are intended to assists students in becoming better writers. Assist with additional duties as needed such as, covering the front desk, scheduling tutoring appointments, answering phones, organizing materials and maintaining information in the ASC . Education, Certifications and/or Licenses High school diploma/ GED required. Successfully completed courses in subject area tutoring with a grade of “A” or “B”. - Successfully demonstrate skills in subject by scoring the minimum required score on grammar and proofing test. - Minimum GPA of 3.0 (exceptions upon discretion of the Director). Experience Formal or informal tutoring experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters pertaining to student’s privacy. Ability to work independently in an efficient manner. Ability to instruct others. Strong interpersonal skills. Demonstrate knowledge and competence in the subject matter. Enjoy tutoring the subject for which services are being provided. Effectively communicate study strategies to ensure academic success. Work comfortably with people from various backgrounds. Exhibit patience and positive attitudes in the learning environment. Ability to provide and demonstrate quality customer service. Pleasant and clearly understandable phone voice. Strong organizational skills to work productively. Ability to adhere to University and departmental policies and procedures. Ability to be discrete in handling confidential matters, while complying with privacy ( FERPA ) regulations. Ability to complete all physical tasks as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you eligible for Work Study? Yes No * Have you completed the course you want to tutor at Texas Wesleyan with an A or B? No Yes Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Transcripts Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://txwes.peopleadmin.com/postings/6472": {
      "title": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Student Activities Student Assistant",
      "description": "Texas Wesleyan University Portal | Student Activities Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Contact Us Student Activities Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications and all supporting materials for this position will only be accepted through the University's online application system. Incomplete applications may not be considered. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Student Activities Student Assistant Position Summary The Student Activities Student Assistant supports the mission of the Office of Student Activities by assisting with the planning, promotion, implementation, and assessment of programs, events, and initiatives that enhance student engagement and campus life. Student Assistants serve as ambassadors for the Division of Student Affairs and contribute to creating a welcoming and vibrant campus community. This position provides hands-on professional experience designed to prepare students for future careers through the development of the National Association of Colleges and Employers ( NACE ) Career Readiness Competencies. Through supervision, mentorship, training, and experiential learning opportunities, Student Assistants gain transferable skills that support academic, personal, and professional success. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Student Engagement and Event Support Assist with the planning, coordination, implementation, and assessment of departmental programs and events, including Stampede Week, Homecoming, Karaoke Nights, Ram Jam, and other campus traditions. Support event logistics including ordering supplies, reserving space, preparing materials, event setup, event management, and breakdown. Encourage student participation and engagement in campus programs, services, organizations, and leadership opportunities. Serve as a positive representative of the Office of Student Activities and Texas Wesleyan University. Welcome and assist students, faculty, staff, alumni, and community guests participating in campus events. Student Organization Support Assist with the planning, maintenance, and administration of RamSpace and related student organization management systems. Support student organizations by maintaining resources, materials, and organizational records. Provide guidance and referrals to student leaders regarding university policies, event planning procedures, and available resources. Be available for consultations with student leaders and organization officers regarding involvement opportunities and organizational success. Marketing and Communication Promote Student Activities programs and services through social media platforms, digital communication, print materials, tabling, and other outreach efforts. Create engaging content that increases student awareness of campus programs and opportunities. Communicate professionally and effectively with diverse audiences through verbal, written, and electronic communication methods. Assist with gathering information, documenting programs, and maintaining departmental communications. Administrative and Operational Support Attend mandatory trainings, staff meetings, and one-on-one meetings with supervisors. Maintain accurate records, inventories, and program documentation. Utilize Microsoft Office, RamSpace, social media platforms, and other university technologies to support departmental operations. Complete assigned projects independently and collaboratively while meeting established timelines and expectations. Support university policies, departmental procedures, and student conduct expectations. Leadership and Professional Development Demonstrate professionalism, accountability, dependability, and ethical decision-making in all work-related responsibilities. Participate actively in professional development opportunities, reflection activities, and skill-building experiences. Seek and apply feedback from supervisors and peers to improve performance and enhance personal and professional growth. Collaborate with fellow Student Assistants and campus partners to achieve departmental goals and improve student experiences. Utilize critical thinking and problem-solving skills to respond to challenges and contribute innovative ideas for program improvement. Foster an environment of belonging, respect, and inclusion for all members of the Texas Wesleyan community. Additional Responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned in support of departmental goals and student success initiatives. Education, Certifications and/or Licenses Must be a currently enrolled Texas Wesleyan University student in good academic standing. Must submit a current semester class schedule as part of the application process. Work availability will be considered as part of the selection process to ensure adequate office coverage, event support, and departmental operations. Students are responsible for providing updated class schedules if course enrollment changes after hire. Must be able to work up to 20 hours per week, depending on departmental needs and supervisor approval. Must maintain availability for scheduled meetings, trainings, programs, and occasional evening or weekend events. Experience Experience in student leadership, event planning, student organizations, customer service, marketing, or campus involvement is preferred but not required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to balance collaborative and independent work. Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, and digital communication skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and general computer systems. Ability to utilize social media and digital communication platforms effectively. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Strong organizational, problem-solving, and critical-thinking skills. Ability to demonstrate professionalism and confidentiality. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds and experiences. Ability to develop creative ideas and contribute innovative solutions. Ability to present information to groups and engage audiences. Ability to attend scheduled meetings, trainings, programs, and events, including occasional evening and weekend commitments. Ability to devote up to 20 hours per week to the position, as determined by the supervisor. Ability to complete physical tasks associated with event setup, breakdown, and office operations. Posting Detail Information Posting Number Posting Open Date 08/10/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Applications and all supporting materials for this position will only be accepted through the University’s online application system. Incomplete applications may not be considered. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please identify any recurring commitments (employment, athletics, organizations, internships, caregiving responsibilities, etc.) that may impact your availability to work during normal business hours (Monday-Friday, 8:00 a.m.-5:00 p.m.). (Open Ended Question) * Do you qualify for work-study funds? Yes No Not sure Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Transcripts Class Schedule (Student Employment Only) List of Three References Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Financial Aid Work Study Award Letter (Student Employment Only) 1201 Wesleyan Street Fort Worth, TX 76105 | 817-531-4444 ©2016 Texas Wesleyan University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
  },
